      "advertised_salary_text": "Immunisation Nurse | Alpine Shire Council Skip to main content Emergency Dashboard Engage Alpine My Alpine Contact Us Residents & Ratepayers Rates & Property Dinner Plain Waste & Recycling Pets & Animals Assets & Roads Trees & Open Spaces Preparing for Emergencies New Residents Community Services Community & Care Local Law Sustainability Grants & Awards Children & Families Youth Services Seniors Facilities Building & Business Building Services Planning Services Strategic Planning Online Maps & Reports Doing Business Running an Event Public & Environmental Health Heritage Information Things to Do Events Calendar Tourism & Visitor Information Swimming & Sports Centres Libraries Volunteer About Us Our Council Council Meetings Our Organisation About Alpine Shire Careers Major Projects Have Your Say Contact Us Preparing for Emergencies Breadcrumb Home About Us Careers Current Vacancies Immunisation Nurse Immunisation Nurse Our Ideal Candidate We are seeking an energetic and engaging individual with previous experience in delivering immunisations and good working knowledge about the National Immunisation Program. The position will work across various locations throughout our council, getting the chance to interact with many of our community members! Sounds like an opportunity for you? See below for more details! Experience & Qualifications: Current and valid nursing registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation (AHPRA). Authorised Immunisation provider. Victorian driver’s licence. Working with Children Check. How You'll Make a Difference Your passion, positive nature and great communication skills will foster an efficient and responsible service to our community. Your professionalism within our small team will help to drive a collaborative and integrated service delivery using contemporary practice, service improvement and excellence to respond to the needs of the community. Join us to deliver immunisations within the Alpine Shire Community. This includes the National Childhood Immunisation Schedule & Secondary School Immunisations Program. Apply Now: Attractive hourly rate of $62.97 - $64.04 (including casual loading) + Allowances + Superannuation. Enjoy the flexibility of casual employment and make the most of our stunning environment. Work across our various facilities across Alpine Shire. Applications close 11 :59pm, 31-May 2026. About Alpine Shire Council Alpine Shire Council is situated in the stunning high-country region of North East Victoria. We are surrounded by spectacular mountains with plenty of natural waterways for you to enjoy. Renowned as one of Victoria’s premier holiday destinations, this spectacular region is an adventure and nature lover’s paradise. Appreciate a perfect work life balance with an adventure, nature and foodie lover’s paradise on your doorstep. Forget about long commutes and paid parking, it’s time for your tree change. Enjoy the rural lifestyle and be welcomed by a friendly community who love where they live and are lucky enough to work close by. Further Questions? Contact Person: Emily Hughes, Maternal & Child Health Nurse Coordinator Phone Number: 03 5755 0555 Alpine Shire Council is an Equal Opportunity employer. People of all abilities, ages, from culturally and/or linguistically diverse backgrounds and First Nations peoples are encouraged to apply for this position. We will provide reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process and in the workplace to support equal opportunities. Please note: Recruitment activity may commence prior to the closing date, so don't delay submitting your application. Council reserves the right to appoint a candidate into the role prior to the closing date. Applicants will be kept updated on the status of their application. Document Position Description - Immunisation Nurse 183.4 KB Apply Now Job Details Work Type Casual Contact Person Emily Hughes Contact Number (03) 5755 0555 Opening Date Friday, 15 Ma