 Lane) – Kent Street Notice of Proposed Sale of Land – Gallagher Lane Ordinary Council Meeting – 26 February 2025 Community Asset Committees - AGM 2025 Home / About Council / Our Organisation / Join us and let's grow together / Application Process Application Process Submit your Application Review the position description on our website and prepare your application including a current copy of your resume and a covering letter. Applications should be submitted via the position application form on our website . Review of Applications After the closing date, a short list of applicants will be selected and invited to attend an interview. If you have been successfully shortlisted you will be contacted via email and/or phone. Interviews Behavioural interviewing techniques and situational questions designed to explore your previous and current work experience, skills and knowledge are utilised during the interview process. In some cases, where a position requires strong teamwork and communication skills, you may be asked to attend a group interview with a number of other candidates. You will also be asked at least one question relating to our Child Safety Policy to assess your ability to support our child safety commitments. If your application progresses to the reference checking stage, a related question will be asked of your referee. Pre-Employment Checks Following the interview process, we will conduct reference checks, a National Criminal History check and Right to Work in Australia check. You will need to provide a current Victorian Working with Children’s Check. Some physical roles will require a pre-employment medical assessment and you may need to provide evidence of mandatory qualifications and memberships, as identified in the Position Description. Offer of Employment The successful candidate will receive a verbal offer of employment from the hiring manager, followed by a formal electronic offer of employment, sent to both their mobile phone and email address. The successful candidate will be asked to complete a health declaration to declare any health conditions or injuries which could or may impact their ability to safely perform their duties. The direct manager would assess potential safety risks and consider reasonable adjustments for employees with pre-existing conditions. Upon acceptance of an employment offer, we will then advise all other applicants of the outcome of their application. Recruitment Timeframes Recruitment Process Estimated Timeframe Advertising period Up to 28 days Shortlisting 1-2 weeks Interviewing 1-2 weeks Pre-employment check process 1-2 weeks Offers of employment 1-5 days Correspondence to unsuccessful candidates 1 week after completion of interview and selection process Back to top Contact Baw Baw Shire Council PO Box 304 Warragul VIC 3820 Toll Free : 1300 BAW BAW (1300 229 229) Tel: +61 3 5624 2411 Fax: +61 3 5622 3654 Email: bawbaw@bawbawshire.vic.gov.au Contact us online now at Enquiries or Complaints . Acknowledgement of Traditional Custodians Council acknowledges the Traditional Custodians and their ongoing connection to the land and waters that make up Baw Baw Shire. We pay our respects to their Elders: past, present, and emerging. We thank the Traditional Custodians for caring for Country and continuing the customs that maintain the longest practised culture in the world. Customer Service Centres 33 Young Street, Drouin WGAC Box Office, Corner of Smith & Albert Streets, Warragul Information and Opening Hours Connect With Us Like us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Council News Watch our YouTube Channel Disclaimer & Copyright | Privacy Statement | Sitemap | Protected Disclosures | Accessibility © 2026 Baw Baw Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
