per Lane) – Kent Street Notice of Proposed Sale of Land – Gallagher Lane Ordinary Council Meeting – 26 February 2025 Community Asset Committees - AGM 2025 Home / About Council / Our Organisation / Join us and let's grow together / Careers in Early Years Careers in Early Years The Victorian Government is investing almost $5 billion over ten years so that children across the state will have access to two years of funded kindergarten programs. This means that an extra year of play-based learning will be added to Victorian children’s education. The learning is led by a teacher. Financial support in the form of scholarships and employment incentives is available for people looking for a rewarding career in the early childhood sector. Three-Year-Old Kindergarten will create more than 6,000 new early childhood education jobs across Victoria, including over 4,000 teachers and 2,000 educators. Baw Baw Shire Council does not employ Early Years Educators directly, but please follow the links for further information or current careers opportunities with registered service providers in the area. Y Kinders Best Chance Early Learning Yarragon Primary School Early Learning Centre Becoming a Family Day Care Educator Family Day Care is a national network of childcare professionals committed to providing a unique, flexible, family focused childcare experience for families. In Baw Baw, we're building family day care into a number one childcare option around and we need your help. If you have experience with children, can provide a warm, secure and family focused environment, and want to build your own successful home based child care business, we would like to hear from you. Complete your expression of interest We are looking for passionate educators! If you are interested in becoming a Family Day Care Educator in Baw Baw Shire, please contact us on (03) 5625 0216 or by email . What Family Day Care offers you Select your own days and hours of work (minimum three weekdays per week) Opportunity to earn a financially rewarding income Manage your business, your income and your work Flexibility, convenience and independence in running your own business from home Develop tailored educational programs for children based on their individual developmental needs, interests and experiences. Regular professional development and training opportunities Regular support and resourcing by friendly and experienced staff. Build long lasting bonds with children and families Network with other likeminded professional FDC educators and staff Thorough and comprehensive orientation process Provide environments that help build children’s connections with the world around them Be a part of a team who is committed to continual improvement Looking to make the move to Baw Baw? find out what makes our region great here! Back to top Contact Baw Baw Shire Council PO Box 304 Warragul VIC 3820 Toll Free : 1300 BAW BAW (1300 229 229) Tel: +61 3 5624 2411 Fax: +61 3 5622 3654 Email: bawbaw@bawbawshire.vic.gov.au Contact us online now at Enquiries or Complaints . Acknowledgement of Traditional Custodians Council acknowledges the Traditional Custodians and their ongoing connection to the land and waters that make up Baw Baw Shire. We pay our respects to their Elders: past, present, and emerging. We thank the Traditional Custodians for caring for Country and continuing the customs that maintain the longest practised culture in the world. Customer Service Centres 33 Young Street, Drouin WGAC Box Office, Corner of Smith & Albert Streets, Warragul Information and Opening Hours Connect With Us Like us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Council News Watch our YouTube Channel Disclaimer & Copyright | Privacy Statement | Sitemap | Protected Disclosures | Accessibility © 2026 Baw Baw Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
