      "advertised_salary_text": "Support Worker (Without Aged Care Certificate) - Bayside, VIC, Australia Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Support Worker (Without Aged Care Certificate) Aged & Disability Part time Closing on: Jun 11 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Part time work that makes a real difference. Salary $32.36 p/h (plus 12% Super) Permanent role No qualifications required Comprehensive training provided Make a meaningful impact in your local community by helping older people live safely and confidently at home. In this hands-on role, you’ll build trusted relationships with clients while providing regular in-home domestic cleaning such as everyday tasks like: Vacuuming, mopping and general cleaning Bathroom and kitchen cleaning Changing bed linen and light laundry Other routine household duties Monitoring the health and wellbeing of clients You’ll visit clients in the local government areas of Bayside Council and Glen Eira Council, bringing not just practical help, but a friendly face and a caring presence. Why Work with Us? Competitive pay aligned with industry standards Minimal travel between clients with paid travel time and kilometre reimbursement Paid sick leave, annual leave and wellbeing leave 🧘‍♀️ Uniforms, mobile phone, cleaning products and equipment provided Regular support from your Team Leader Free digital foreshore parking permit at all council beach carparks in Bayside 🏖️ Enjoy the security and stability of working for local government. Flexible days and hours Build a regular roster of regular clients for a more meaningful work experience What do we need from you? Be able to work at least 4 weekdays between 9am to 3pm Your own reliable car and a valid Victorian driver’s license A clear police check and working with children check (we will pay for these) Able to meet the physical requirements of the role If you enjoy helping others, love a tidy space, and want a job that feels good at the end of the day, this is f