e on Facebook Share on Twitter Print Content components School crossing supervisors have a much-valued role in Boroondara. On an average school day in Boroondara, they help 9,266 pedestrians to cross the street while 74,426 motor vehicles use our roads during school crossing times. We are always looking for school crossing supervisors. If you are friendly, reliable and flexible, this role is for you. What does a school crossing supervisor do? This paid position gives you the opportunity to get involved in your community and improve road safety for children, people with a disability and the general public who use our 114 school crossings. School crossing supervisors: • work part-time Monday to Friday, from 8 am to 9 am and from 3 pm to 4 pm, during the school term • play an important role in educating children with ‘Stop, Look and Listen’ instructions • are responsible for reporting any road hazards or potential risks • help to encourage active and independent travel. About you We are looking for people aged 18 and older who: • can attend shifts at short notice • have their own reliable transport • are able to work across several locations • can complete the pre-employment medical and police checks. You will have access to a full training program before starting your role. Download the position description School Crossing Supervisor PD 144.04 KB [PDF] 23 November 2022 How to apply Learn more about this rewarding role by reading the position description above. Submit an online application through our Careers website . Attend an interview – meet with one of our Council Officers at Council, located at 8 Inglesby Road in Camberwell. Provide us with relevant employment documents – including your Working With Children Check, Police Check and evidence of your COVID-19 vaccination status. Complete a medical assessment. Apply to become a School Crossings Supervisor We are always recruiting new school crossing supervisors to help people to cross our roads safely at peak school times. More information Call (03) 9278 4774 or email [email protected] for more information. Careers at Boroondara Learn more about what it's like to work with us. Learn more Was this page helpful? Yes No 8 Inglesby Road, Camberwell, Victoria 3124 (opens in a new window) The City of Boroondara acknowledges the Wurundjeri Woi-wurrung people as the Traditional Owners and original custodians of this land, and we pay our respects to their Elders past and present. Facebook (opens in a new window) Twitter (opens in a new window) YouTube (opens in a new window) LinkedIn (opens in a new window) Instagram (opens in a new window) Quick links Bin day Hard waste collection Planning permit register Parking fines Pet registration Explore local Events and activities Libraries Parks and reserves Markets and shopping Spaces, venues and facilities Your Council Jobs and careers News Council meetings Your Councillors Policies, plans and strategies Back to top Sitemap Disclaimer Terms and Conditions Privacy Statement Accessibility © City of Boroondara 2026, All Rights Reserved. Become a school crossing supervisor and play an important role in our community. City of Boroondara https://www.boroondara.vic.gov.au/your-council/jobs-and-careers-boroondara/become-school-crossing-supervisor Become a school crossing supervisor Become a school crossing supervisor and play an important role in our community. no-reply@boroondara.vic.gov.au en_GB Thu 13 September 2018 Fri 14 November 2025 City of Boroondara City of Boroondara Collection en-AU summary Become a school crossing supervisor and play an important role in our community. Become a school crossing supervisor Drupal 10 (https://www.drupal.org) width true width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0 width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0 Utility links secondary menu toggle Utility links (mobile) Breadcrumb Listen to this page using ReadSpeaker Careers website Apply to become a School Crossings Supervisor Quick links footer menu Explore local footer me