      "closing_date": "2026-06-26",
      "closing_text": "Career Opportunities: Tree Crew Supervisor (15022) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Tree Crew Supervisor (15022) Requisition ID 15022 - Posted - Job Function (1) - Tenure Status (1) - Employment Status (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Full time role, to lead and organise Tree Crew operations, located in Kew $86,620 - $100,054 plus super and allowances 9 day fortnight, plus tool of trade vehicle The Opportunity We are seeking a dedicated and experienced Tree Crew Supervisor to join our Open Space and Trees team. This is a critical role in leading the daily operations of Council’s Tree Crew, ensuring the delivery of safe, high-quality arboricultural services. T Key Responsibilities Arrange responses to urgent requests Manage a small crew to provide a positive and engaged team culture, that operations safely and in compliance with relevant legislation Manage the maintenance and replacement of Tree Crew plant and equipment Arrange contractors, issue work orders Provide a high level of customer service, and detailed record keeping. We are seeking someone: Experienced in tree maintenance, pruning and removals. Strong leadership skills; able to motivate and support staff. Confident managing high workloads and frequent customer contact. Effective communicator who builds good working relationships. Organised, safety‐focused and able to manage competing priorities. Comfortable interpreting legislation and using digital systems. For more information, please refer to the position description Employment Requirements Applicants must hold unrestricted working rights in Australia, and those progressing through the selection process will need to complete a National Police Record Check, a Working with Children Check and relevant pre-employment medical assessments. How to apply Please submit your application online via the ‘Apply Now’ button by Friday 26th June 2026 . All applications must be made via the online portal; no applications direct to the hiring manager or from recruitment agencies will be considered. For a confidential discussion about this position please contact Darren Bowtell, Senior Arborist, Reactive Maintenance on (03) 9278 4444 during business hours or email darren.bowtell@boroondara.vic.gov.au Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel 1U1FMVD02OSZDQ09OPTAmRldSPTAmTlJFPTAmQ0VYVD0wJlNUPTE3ODI0MTgxNDI5ODgmRUlEPUVWRU5ULVVOS05PV04tVU5LTk9XTi1vYjU1YWJicTAxMTYtMjAyNjA2MjUyMDA5MDItMTg2NDM4NiZDTE9DPTAmQ1JFTT0wJk5XUj0wJkNQVT0xNzQmU1ZUPTI4MyZTUUxDPTk1JlNDUFU9MCZDU1VQPTM5Jk1FTT0zMDI3NiZVQ1BVPTE3NCZGUkU9MCZUT0s9MTA0RjU4NDUxMUY1QjQxNjVGQTI= {\"xweb/ecsnack-content\":{\"resourceMapping\":{\"xweb/ecsnack-content/i18n/messagebundle.properties\":\"/messagebundle/cityofboroP/vmod_v1-351608f-f3980725/verp/ui/ecsnack-content/resources/i18n/messagebundle.properties\",\"xweb/common-messagebundles/i18n/common-components/messagebundle.properties\":\"/messagebundle/cityofboroP/vmod_v1-3b447c26-f3980725/verp/ui/common-messagebundles/resources/i18n/common-components/messagebundle.properties\"},\"manifest\":{\"async\":true,\"entrypoints\":[\"static/css/main.4f427dfa.css\",\"static/js/main.8f269b16.js\"]},\"root\":{\"url\":\"/verp/vmod_v1/ui/ecsnack-content/resources_5.8.0/\"}},\"xweb/global-header\":{\"resourceMapping\":{\"xweb/common-messagebundles/i18n/common-components/messagebundle.properties\":\"/messagebundle/cityofboroP/vmod_v1-3b447c26-f3980725/verp/ui/common-messagebundles/resources/i18n/common-components/messagebundle.properties\",\"xweb/global-header/i18n/messagebundle.properties\":\"/messagebundle/cityofboroP/vmod_v1-7f0831dc-f3980725/verp/u