      "closing_date": "2026-06-07",
      "closing_text": "Career Opportunities: Insurance Officer (15105) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Insurance Officer (15105) Requisition ID 15105 - Posted - Job Function (1) - Tenure Status (1) - Employment Status (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Insurance Officer Join Council’s Governance and Legal Department Be part of a supportive and collaborative team Full-time, ongoing position $84,770 - $98,205 per annum plus super and RDO We are seeking a capable and community-minded Insurance Officer to join Council’s Governance and Legal Department. In this role, you will manage a broad range of insurance claims, contribute to risk and assurance activities, and help deliver fair, timely and well-informed outcomes for Council and the community. About you We are looking for someone who is passionate about providing outstanding service and making a positive impact in the community. You will bring: A strong understanding of insurance claims management and tort law principles, ideally within a government setting Excellent written communication skills, with the ability to write clear and accurate responses Strong attention to detail, helping you process claims thoroughly and on time A customer-focused approach and a collaborative mindset – you enjoy working with others to achieve the best outcomes Confidence using multiple systems and tools to manage your work efficiently Key responsibilities The primary role of the Insurance Officer is to process claims made against Council. Claims can include damage from Council trees and trucks, personal injury, water flow, and professional liability. You will investigate incidents, draft correspondence, and advocate for outcomes in the best interest of Council and the community. You will also manage some court claims, assisting Council’s insurer and their lawyers. Additionally, you will coordinate the discovery process for litigated claims and manage Freedom of Information requests. As part of the Risk and Assurance team within Council’s Governance and Legal Department, the role also assists with: Crisis management coordination Maintaining Council’s Business Continuity Plans Implementing and managing Council's Risk Management Framework and enterprise risk register Council’s insurance renewal program Fraud and corruption control What sets us apart? An investment in your ongoing professional and personal development. A supportive and friendly workplace culture that values diversity, collaboration and continuous improvement. We offer many staff benefits such as flexible working arrangements, study support, wellbeing programs, gym and pool memberships. Employment requirements Applicants must have the right to work in Australia Preferred applicants will be required to undergo a National Police Record Check How to apply Please submit your application online via the ‘Apply’ button by Sunday 7 June 2026, 11:59pm . All applications must be made via the online portal. For further information, please view the position description . For a confidential discussion about this position please contact Rudi Dellow on (03) 9278 4686 during business hours. We understand that this portal may not meet the needs of people who rely on Assistive Technology or have other diverse requirements. If you have any difficulty using our recruitment system, please do not hesitate to contact People Culture and Development on (03) 9278 4401 or pcd@boroondara.vic.gov.au to allow us to help in any way we can. Who are we? The City of Boroondara is a metropolitan council, representing more than 170,000 people in the inner-eastern suburbs of Melbourne. A leader in the local government sector, with a reputation for innovation and excellence, we believe in providing an environment where our staff thrive, both in the work they do and in how they learn and develop as people and professionals. We like to challenge the norm and we are investing significantly in innovation and technology improvements in order to provide our customers with an even greater experience and engagement. We are putting our customers at the forefront of what we do with our organisation wide initiative, Transforming Boroondara Program. You will be instrumental in driving this change across the organisation using best practice approaches to successfully support us from the now to our desired future state. With so much going on it’s a great time to join Boroondara! #S-DNI Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel 1U1FMVD0xMTgmQ0NPTj0yJkZXUj0wJk5SRT0wJkNFWFQ9MCZTVD0xNzgwNDc2OTc2NDI2JkVJRD1FVkVOVC1VTktOT1dOLVVOS05PV04tb2I1NWFiYnEwMTA1LTIwMjYwNjAzMDg1NjE2LTk2Nzk0NSZDTE9DPTEmQ1JFTT0wJk5XUj0wJkNQVT0yNzUmU1ZUPTQ2NyZTUUxDPTEzMSZTQ1BVPTAmQ1NVUD05NiZNRU09MzkwNTImVUNQVT0yNzUmRlJFPTAmVE9LPUJEQTJBRDc0MjVGMEY5NjkwNzE1 {\"xweb/ecsnack-content\":{\"resourceMapping\":{\"xweb/ecsnack-content/i18n/messagebundle.properties\":\"/messagebundle/cityofboroP/vmod_v1-feaa8ded-f3980725/verp/ui/ecsnack-content/resources/i18n/messagebundle.properties\",\"xweb/common-messagebundles/i18n/common-components/messagebundle.properties\":\"/messagebundle/cityofboroP/vmod_v1-c6bf9144-f3980725/verp/ui/common-messagebundles/resources/i18n/common-components/messagebundle.properties\"},\"manifest\":{\"async\":true,\"entrypoints\":[\"static/css/main.4f427dfa.css\",\"static/js/main.8f269b16.js\"]},\"root\":{\"url\":\"/verp/vmod_v1/ui/ecsnack-content/resources_5.8.0/\"}},\"xweb/global-header\":{\"resourceMapping\":{\"xweb/common-messagebundles/i18n/common-components/messagebundle.properties\":\"/messagebundle/cityofboroP/vmod_v1-c6bf9144-f3980725/verp/ui/common-messagebundles/resources/i18n/common-