 employee assistance program, health and wellbeing programs and excellent leave entitlements. If you can’t find the right job, create your candidate profile and set up job alert emails so you don't miss out on current opportunities. Create or view your candidate profile Latest opportunities Displaying 4 of 4 job Volunteer Sector Development Officer Type Full-time Duration Fixed term contract until 30 June 2027 Salary $84,770 to $98,205 per year (plus super and RDO) Play a key role to promote and raise the profile of volunteering across Boroondara. Application close Wed 10 June 2026 View job details Change Analyst Type Full-time Duration Fixed term position (until 16 July 2027) Salary $114,259 to $127,587 per year pro rata (plus super and RDO) We are seeking a proactive Change Analyst to support the delivery of meaningful, organisation-wide transformation. Application close Tue 9 June 2026 View job details Transfer Station Attendant Operator Type Full-time Duration Ongoing Salary $86,472 (plus super) We are seeking an Attendant Operator to work in our Transfer Station and Yard Maintenance team, which is located at the Boroondara Waste and Recycling Centre. The team is responsible for the receiving, organising and cartage of hard, household, recyclable and organic waste. Our team members enjoy variety of work in a very busy operational work site which is open 7 days a week. Application close Sun 7 June 2026 View job details Waste Attendant (Multiple Positions) Type Full-time Duration Ongoing Salary $80,129 (plus super) Contribute your teamwork and customer-oriented skills to an already great team of Waste Drivers and Waste Attendants. Application close Sun 7 June 2026 View job details See all jobs Meet our people What makes Boroondara such a great place to work? Hear from a group of our passionate people. Learn more about our people The values that drive our work Our set of values reflect what is important to us and the behaviours that we hold ourselves accountable to. Our purpose of 'working together to deliver community priorities and placing our customers at the centre of everything we do' is one of the top reasons people choose to work here. Learn more about our values on Our values page . Our commitment to diversity and inclusion We are committed to providing a safe culture where employees from diverse backgrounds can bring their whole selves to work. Download our Gender Equality Action Plan 2022–25 below to find out more about the actions we will take to progress gender equality. The City of Boroondara is also committed to providing systems that are accessible to as many people as possible. We understand that this portal may not meet the needs of people who rely on assistive technology or have other diverse requirements. If you have any difficulty using our recruitment system, please do not hesitate to contact People Culture and Development on (03) 9278 4401 or email [email protected] to allow us to help in any way we can. Download our Gender Equality Action Plan Gender Equality Action Plan 2022-25 1.06 MB [PDF] 29 August 2022 Enterprise Agreement View our Enterprise Agreement 2024 on the Fair Work Commission website . Salary schedules within the agreement are based on 2024 figures. Child pages View current job vacancies Find out about the latest job opportunities available at the City of Boroondara. How to apply Learn about our job application process. Benefits of working with us Work with us and get access to some fantastic benefits. Our values Learn about the values that drive how employees at Boroondara City Council work and lead. Apply for work experience Put your coursework into practice and gain insight into working at Council. Become a school crossing supervisor Become a school crossing supervisor and play an important role in our community. Work-life balance Learn more about flexible working arrangements. Meet our people Find out what our employees like most about working at Boroondara. Was this page helpful? Yes 