o apply Benefits of working with us Our values Apply for work experience Become a school crossing supervisor Work-life balance Meet our people Contact us Projects and major works History and demographics Community awards and ceremonies Community Satisfaction Survey Boroondara new residents' guide View current job vacancies Listen Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Print Content components We offer a wide range of roles and value different skills at Boroondara. Have a look at the latest job openings and reach out to the contact person listed in the job ad if you would like more information. We also recognise the benefits of a diverse workforce at Boroondara and promote equity of access to employment opportunities. If you need support to access job information or have more questions, email us at [email protected] or phone (03) 9278 4401 . To make sure you don't miss out on current opportunities, create your candidate profile and set up job alert emails. Create or view your candidate profile Volunteer Sector Development Officer Type Full-time Duration Fixed term contract until 30 June 2027 Salary $84,770 to $98,205 per year (plus super and RDO) Play a key role to promote and raise the profile of volunteering across Boroondara. Application close Wed 10 June 2026 View job details Change Analyst Type Full-time Duration Fixed term position (until 16 July 2027) Salary $114,259 to $127,587 per year pro rata (plus super and RDO) We are seeking a proactive Change Analyst to support the delivery of meaningful, organisation-wide transformation. Application close Tue 9 June 2026 View job details Transfer Station Attendant Operator Type Full-time Duration Ongoing Salary $86,472 (plus super) We are seeking an Attendant Operator to work in our Transfer Station and Yard Maintenance team, which is located at the Boroondara Waste and Recycling Centre. The team is responsible for the receiving, organising and cartage of hard, household, recyclable and organic waste. Our team members enjoy variety of work in a very busy operational work site which is open 7 days a week. Application close Sun 7 June 2026 View job details Waste Attendant (Multiple Positions) Type Full-time Duration Ongoing Salary $80,129 (plus super) Contribute your teamwork and customer-oriented skills to an already great team of Waste Drivers and Waste Attendants. Application close Sun 7 June 2026 View job details Senior Building Surveyor Type Part-time Duration Ongoing position (32 hours per week) Salary $150,113 to $161,348 per year, pro rata to be applied (plus super) Contribute to high-quality regulatory outcomes for our community. Application close Mon 1 June 2026 View job details Senior Place and Design Officer Type Full-time Duration Full-time, ongoing position Salary $101,985 to $110,964 (plus super, plus monthly RDO) This is an exciting opportunity to provide planning and design services for shopping centres, open spaces, playgrounds and other Council projects. Application close Mon 8 June 2026 View job details Horticultural Specialist Type Full-time Duration Ongoing Salary $71,312 to $76,789 (plus super plus 9-day fortnight) Help shape and maintain Boroondara’s beautiful parks, gardens and streetscapes for the community to enjoy every day. Application close Sun 7 June 2026 View job details Local Laws Officer Type Full-time Duration Ongoing position Salary $91,334 to $98,476 per year (plus super) Join us in building a professional investigations team and help deliver a responsive, community-focused Local Laws service. Application close Sun 31 May 2026 View job details Arts Cultural Development Officer Type Full-time Duration 3 months Salary $101,985 to $110,964 Reporting to the Senior Coordinator Community & Cultural Programming, you will be responsible for supporting the investigation, development and delivery of innovative creative programs, events and services to ensure quality cultural development outcomes for our Boroondara community. Application close Thu 28 May 2026 View job details Waste Driver / Attendant Type Full-time Duration Ongoing Salary $90,430 per year (plus superannuation) We are seeking Waste Driver / Attendant to work in our Waste Operations team, which is located at the Boroondara Waste and Recycling Centre operated by the City of Boroondara. The team is responsible for weekday collection of hard, household, recyclable and organic waste. Our team members enjoy a variety of work in densely populated residential areas and in a very busy operational work site. If you have experience in the Waste industry, we welcome your application. Application close Sun 17 May 2026 View job details Casual School Crossing Supervisor Type Casual Duration Casual Position Salary $42.11 per hour, includes 25% casual loading, plus superannuation We are inviting expressions of interest from people who may be suitable for future School Crossing Supervisor opportunities. While this is not an active recruitment process, it enables Council to identify suitable candidates for future opportunities as they arise across the municipality. Application close Tue 30 June 2026 View job details Casual Maternal and Child Health (MCH) Nurse Type Casual Duration Casual Salary $61.82 to $66.58 plus 25% loading per hour Casual MCH Nurses required Application close Thu 31 December 2026 View job details School Crossing Supervisor Type Part-time Duration Ongoing Salary $11,125 per year (plus super) Become an appreciated Council employee — we value diversity, inclusion, belonging, feedback and continuous improvement. Help students and families cross the road safely during peak school times. Application close Tue 30 June 2026 View job details Child pages Was this page helpful? Yes No 8 Inglesby Road, Camberwell, Victoria 3124 (opens in a new window) The City of Boroondara acknowledges the Wurundjeri Woi-wurrung people as the Traditional Owners and original custodians of this land, and we pay our respects to their Elders past and present. Facebook (opens in a ne