      "closing_date": "2026-08-23",
      "closing_text": "Career Opportunities: Park Asset Specialist (15178) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Park Asset Specialist (15178) Requisition ID 15178 - Posted - Job Function (2) - Tenure Status (1) - Employment Status (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List $73,273 to $78,901 (ongoing, full time, plus superannuation, 9 day fortnight) Build and maintain the parks and playgrounds that our community enjoys every day Work outdoors across some of Melbourne's most valued parks and reserves The Role Reporting to the Parks Team Leader, the Park Asset Specialist plays an important role in maintaining the safety, functionality and presentation of Council's playgrounds, park furniture and associated infrastructure. Based at Kew Depot and working across the municipality, this hands-on role is responsible for delivering maintenance and repair services that ensure our parks and open spaces remain safe, attractive and welcoming for the community. You will undertake a variety of maintenance activities, inspections and repair works while working collaboratively with colleagues, contractors and members of the public. Key Responsibilities Carry out maintenance, repairs and minor construction works across playgrounds, park furniture and fence assets within Council's open spaces. Undertake routine playground inspections and audits to ensure compliance with relevant Australian Standards and identify any safety concerns. Arrange for hazards and defects to be repaired, replaced or made safe in a timely manner, ensuring community safety remains a priority. Plan and complete maintenance works while considering the horticultural amenity and presentation of park sites, leaving work areas clean and safe upon completion . About You You will bring practical experience in outdoor maintenance, construction, landscaping, carpentry or a related field, together with a strong commitment to safety and high-quality workmanship. You have experience installing, repairing and maintaining outdoor furniture, structures or timber assets and enjoy working in a physically active outdoor environment. You are self-motivated, organised and capable of managing your workload while responding to changing priorities. Your ability to work both independently and as part of a team, combined with strong communication skills, will enable you to build positive relationships with colleagues and the community. Qualifications or experience in carpentry, landscaping, welding, forklift operation or medium rigid vehicle operation will be highly regarded. For more information regarding the role, please refer to the attached position description. About Boroondara The City of Boroondara is home to some of Melbourne's most beautiful parks, playgrounds, gardens and open spaces. We are committed to creating a healthy, connected and sustainable community and delivering services that place our customers at the centre of everything we do. As one of Melbourne's most desirable municipalities, we take pride in maintaining high quality public spaces that support recreation, wellbeing and community connection. Working with us means contributing to assets and environments that are enjoyed by thousands of residents and visitors each year. Employment Requirements Applicants must hold unrestricted working rights in Australia, and those progressing through the selection process will need to complete a National Police Record Check, a Working with Children Check and relevant pre-employment medical assessments. How to Apply Please submit your application online via the 'Apply' button by 11.59pm, Sunday 23 August 2026. All applications must be made via the online portal; no applications direct to the hiring manager or from recruitment agencies will be considered. For a confidential discussion about this position please conta