    {
      "advertised_salary_max": 98205.0,
      "advertised_salary_min": 84770.0,
      "advertised_salary_period": "year",
      "advertised_salary_text": "$84,770 to $98,205 (pro rata to be applied) per annum plus Superannuation Make a difference by coordinating",
      "band": 5,
      "classification_status": "explicit_band",
      "closing_date": "2026-06-21",
      "closing_text": "Career Opportunities: Safer Communities Project Officer (15090) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Safer Communities Project Officer (15090) Requisition ID 15090 - Posted - Job Function (1) - Tenure Status (1) - Employment Status (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Safer Communities Project Officer Play a key role in promoting community safety and fostering participation in community life. Part time, fixed term position for 4 months (23 hours per week). $84,770 to $98,205 (pro rata to be applied) per annum plus Superannuation Make a difference by coordinating and delivering a variety of projects and events with a focus on fostering participation in community life and promoting community safety. A little bit about the role Reporting to the Health Planning Team Leader, the Safer Communities Project Officer will be responsible for assisting with the delivery of a variety of projects and community events such as Community Safety Month (including the Emergency Family Fun Day and Community Safety Forum), International Women’s Day, 16 Days of Activism Against Gender Based Violence Campaign, and Homelessness Week. The role will also support delivery of projects in the health and wellbeing space, and the implementation of Council’s Homelessness Protocol, as required. This includes supporting the Safer Communities Planner (Homelessness) to coordinate Council’s approach to managing complex issues relating to health and safety issues that may arise at sites where people are sleeping rough in the municipality. A little bit about you You will have outstanding communication skills, both written and verbal, be personable and approachable and able to engage with a range of audiences including, external agencies and groups, Victorian Government departments, service providers, and the community. You will have a demonstrated understanding of health, wellbeing and safety issues impacting the community, for example family violence and homelessness. You will have experience in project development and the delivery of community events. You will also have comprehensive computer skills across the Microsoft Office range of applications, a willingness to work as part of a team and prepared to share experiences with other team members to improve overall knowledge. The successful incumbent will also have: post-secondary qualifications with relevant work experience a commitment to quality outcomes and efficient work practices, and excellent time management and organisation skills Employment Requirements Applicants must have the right to work in Australia. Preferred applicants will be required to undergo a National Police Record Check and hold a valid Working with Children Clearance. How to Apply Please submit your application online via the ‘ Apply’ button by 11:59pm Sunday 21 June 2026 . All applications must be made via the online portal; no applications direct to the hiring manager will be considered. For any further information please refer to the position description , or contact Katherine Wright (Senior Coordinator Social Planning & Research) during business hours on 9278 4827 for a confidential discussion. We understand that this portal may not meet the needs of people who rely on Assistive Technology or have other diverse requirements. If you have any difficulty using our recruitment system, please do not hesitate to contact People Culture and Development on (03) 9278 4401 or pcd@boroondara.vic.gov.au to allow us to help in any way we can. Who are we? The City of Boroondara is a metropolitan council, representing more than 170,000 people in the inner-eastern suburbs of Melbourne. A leader in the local government sector, with a reputation for innovation and excellence, we believe in providing an environment where our staff thrive, both in the work they do and in how they learn and develop as people and professionals. We like to challenge the norm and we are investing significantly in innovation and technology improvements in order to provide our customers with an even greater experience and engagement. We are putting our customers at the forefront of what we do with our organisation wide initiative, Transforming Boroondara Program. You will be instrumental in driving this change across the organisation using best practice approaches to successfully support us from the now to our desired future state. With so much going on it’s a great time to join Boroondara! #S-DNI Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel 1U1FMVD0xMDgmQ0NPTj0yJkZXUj0wJk5SRT0wJkNFWFQ9MCZTVD0xNzgxOTg0NzE3NjUxJkVJRD1FVkVOVC1VTktOT1dOLVVOS05PV04tb2I1NWFiYnEwMTA1LTIwMjYwNjIwMTk0NTE3LTU1Nzg3MiZDTE9DPTEmQ1JFTT0wJk5XUj0wJkNQVT0yNjUmU1ZUPTQ1NSZTUUxDPTEzMSZTQ1BVPTAmQ1NVUD05OSZNRU09MzgxODcmVUNQVT0yNjUmRlJFPTAmVE9LPUEwODE5NTQ4NDVGRDAxRkYwQjVG {\"xweb/ecsnack-content\":{\"resourceMapping\":{\"xweb/ecsnack-content/i18n/messagebundle.properties\":\"/messagebundle/cityofboroP/vmod_v1-351608f-f3980725/verp/ui/ecsnack-content/resources/i18n/messagebundle.properties\",\"xweb/common-messagebundles/i18n/common-components/messagebundle.properties\":\"/messagebundle/cityofboroP/vmod_v1-3b447c26-f3980725/verp/ui/common-messagebundles/resources/i18n/common-components/messagebundle.properties\"},\"manifest\":{\"async\":true,\"entrypoints\":[\"static/css/main.4f427dfa.css\",\"static/js/main.8f269b16.js\"]},\"root\":{\"url\":\"/verp/vmod_v1/ui/ecsnack-content/resources_5.8.0/\"}},\"xweb/global-header\":{\"resourceMapping\":{\"xweb/common-messagebundles/i18n/common-components/messagebundle.properties\":\"/messagebundle/cityofboroP/vmod_v1-3b447c26-f3980725/verp/ui/common-mess