      "band": 6,
      "classification_status": "explicit_band",
      "closing_date": "2026-06-08",
      "closing_text": "Career Opportunities: Senior Place and Design Officer (15095) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Senior Place and Design Officer (15095) Requisition ID 15095 - Posted - Job Function (1) - Tenure Status (1) - Employment Status (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Deliver meaningful public realm and other projects across one of Melbourne’s most liveable municipalities Ongoing, full time, opportunity based in Camberwell with flexible work arrangements $101,985 to $110,964 (plus super and monthly RDO) About Boroondara The City of Boroondara is recognised for its vibrant neighbourhoods, heritage character and high-quality public spaces. Our vision is to be a thriving, inclusive city that meets the needs and aspirations of our community. Guided by strong values and a customer-first mindset, we work collaboratively to deliver places and services that enhance liveability for residents, businesses and visitors. About the Role We are seeking a Senior Place and Design Officer to join our Landscape and Design team within the Capital Projects department. In this role, you will contribute to the planning, design and delivery of high-quality public realm projects across shopping centres, streets, parks, playgrounds and open spaces. You will play a key role in shaping places that are functional, sustainable and reflective of Boroondara’s unique character, while balancing community needs and strategic priorities. Key Responsibilities You will lead the development of public realm design solutions from concept through to construction documentation, ensuring designs meet community expectations and industry standards. The role involves managing projects end-to-end, including budgets, timelines and multidisciplinary teams, as well as contributing to strategic planning, policy development and open space master planning. You will work closely with stakeholders to deliver innovative, well-considered outcomes and ensure effective consultation and communication across projects. You will also foster strong partnerships with internal teams, consultants, contractors, businesses and the community, ensuring project outcomes align with Council’s vision while enhancing user experience and satisfaction. About You You are an experienced and creative professional with a background in landscape architecture, urban design or project management. You bring strong expertise in placemaking, public realm design and community consultation, along with demonstrated experience delivering projects from inception to completion. Your strengths include stakeholder engagement, problem solving and the ability to manage competing priorities while maintaining attention to detail. You are a collaborative team player with excellent communication skills and a proactive approach to innovation and continuous improvement. Your passion for creating great public spaces and your commitment to delivering community-focused outcomes will see you succeed in this role. If you’d like to know more about the role, please see the position description. Employment Requirements Applicants must hold unrestricted working rights in Australia, and those progressing through the selection process will need to complete a National Police Record Check, and may also require a Working with Children Check and any relevant pre-employment medical assessments as per the specific position description requirements. How to Apply Please submit your application online via the ‘ Apply’ button by 11.59pm Monday 8 June 2026 . All applications must be made via the online portal; no applications direct to the hiring manager or from recruitment agencies will be considered. For a confidential discussion about this position please contact Nathan Milesi Coordinator, Landscape & Design on 03 9278 4444 during business hours or nathan.milesi@boroondara.vic.gov.au I f you wa nt to know more about the benefits of working for the City of Boroondara, please visit our careers website boroondara.vic.gov.au/careers The City of Boroondara is committed to providing systems that are accessible to as many people as possible. We understand that this portal may not meet the needs of people who rely on Assistive Technology or have other diverse requirements. If you have any difficulty using our recruitment system, please do not hesitate to contact People Culture and Development on (03) 9278 4401 or pcd@boroondara.vic.gov.au to allow us to help in any way we can. Council recognises the benefits of a diverse workforce for its employees and customers. To ensure equity of access to employment opportunities, Council encourages applications from underrepresented groups including people who are from an Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander background, people from different ages, abilities, gender identities, sexual orientation and cultural backgrounds. If you require any additional support or adjustments regarding interview arrangements, please advise the contact listed above in advance. Council is a child safe organisation and as such, some positions may require the incumbent to hold a Working with Children Check. Working together We are currently undertaking an exciting project that will see a transformation in the way we work and the way we serve our customers. Implementation of the Transforming Boroondara Program will provide a customer centric model of service delivery that includes technological innovation, process improvement and business system renewal - we value your input and look forward to our journey ahead. #S-DNI Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel  {\"xweb/ecsnack-content\":{\"resourceMapping\":{\"x