      "closing_date": "2026-07-12",
      "closing_text": "Career Opportunities: Senior Project Manager (15109) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Senior Project Manager (15109) Requisition ID 15109 - Posted - Job Function (1) - Tenure Status (1) - Employment Status (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Be a part of the exciting Capital Projects team with hybrid working options available Ongoing, full-time opportunity available $114,259 - $127,587 Band 7 plus superannuation plus monthly RDO At the City of Boroondara, we’re proud of our vibrant, sustainable and inclusive community. As an organisation, we work together to deliver meaningful outcomes and place our customers at the centre of everything we do. We are currently seeking a skilled and passionate Senior Project Manager to join our Capital Projects team and play a vital role in shaping the future of our built environment. About the Role As a Senior Project Manager, you will take the lead in delivering complex capital building and infrastructure projects across our municipality. From concept through to completion, you will manage all stages of project delivery—working closely with internal stakeholders, external contractors and consultants, and the broader Boroondara community. This is a dynamic and rewarding role that places you at the forefront of enhancing community spaces and delivering high-quality public infrastructure. Key Responsibilities In this role, you will be responsible for preparing detailed project scopes and estimates in collaboration with internal departments and managing projects from initial planning through to successful delivery. You will apply sound project management principles to ensure projects are completed on time, within budget and to the highest standard, while effectively managing risk, quality and stakeholder expectations. You will oversee all aspects of contract management including the preparation of tenders, contractor selection and performance monitoring, in line with Council’s governance and procurement frameworks. Communication is key—whether leading project working groups, presenting to stakeholders or preparing clear, plain-language reports for Council decision-making. Environmental sustainability will be a focus in your planning and design, aligning with Boroondara’s strategic goals. About You You are a highly experienced project manager with a relevant tertiary qualification in Project Management, Engineering, Architecture or a similar field. You bring demonstrated success in delivering complex community infrastructure projects and have a strong understanding of construction contract management, budgeting, stakeholder engagement and risk mitigation. Your communication skills are exceptional, enabling you to confidently lead teams, resolve challenges and engage effectively with diverse groups. You thrive in a collaborative environment and are driven by a genuine desire to improve outcomes for the community. You are detail-oriented, strategic and solutions-focused, with a passion for excellence in service delivery. Employment requirements Applicants must have unlimited work rights to work in Australia. Preferred applicants will be required to undergo a National Police Record Check and Working with Children Check. If you would like to know more about the role, please refer to the position description. How to Apply Please submit your application online via the ‘Apply’ button by 11.59pm, Sunday 12 July 2026 . All applications must be made via the online portal; no applications direct to the hiring manager will be considered. No calls or applications from agencies please. For a confidential discussion about this position please contact Jarrod Filosa , Coordinator Building Projects on 0422 386 630 or jarrod.filosa@boroondara.vic.gov.au during business hours. I f you wa nt to know more about the benefits of working for the City of Boroondara, please visit our careers website boroondara.vic.gov.au/careers The City of Boroondara is committed to providing systems that are accessible to as many people as possible. We understand that this portal may not meet the needs of people who rely on Assistive Technology or have other diverse requirements. If you have any difficulty using our recruitment system, please do not hesitate to contact People Culture and Development on (03) 9278 4401 or pcd@boroondara.vic.gov.au to allow us to help in any way we can. Council recognises the benefits of a diverse workforce for its employees and customers. To ensure equity of access to employment opportunities, Council encourages applications from underrepresented groups including people who are from an Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander background, people from different ages, abilities, gender identities, sexual orientation and cultural backgrounds. If you require any additional support or adjustments regarding interview arrangements, please advise the contact listed above in advance. Council is a child safe organisation and as such, some positions may require the incumbent to hold a Working with Children Check. Working together We are currently undertaking an exciting project that will see a transformation in the way we work and the way we serve our customers. Implementation of the Transforming Boroondara Program will provide a customer centric model of service delivery that includes technological innovation, process improvement and business system renewal - we value your input and look forward to our journey ahead. #S-DNI Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel 1U1FMVD04NyZDQ09OPTImRldSPTAmTlJFPTAmQ0VYVD0wJlNUPTE3ODM3OTcxMDg0MzkmRUlEPUVWRU5ULVVOS05PV04tVU5LTk9XTi1vYjU1YWJicTAxMDU