      "advertised_salary_max": 203.0,
      "advertised_salary_min": 21.0,
      "advertised_salary_period": "year",
      "advertised_salary_text": "Careers Campaspe Shire Council opens in new tab or window Skip to main content Menu Search Home Our services Aged care & disability Community transport Parking permits Community directory Animals Campaspe Animal Services Animals & pets Children & families Centre-based child care Immunisations Kindergartens Playgroups & Occasional Care Child Safety Community support & programs Access & inclusion Citizen of the Year Community directory First Peoples communities & culture Grants & letters of support Healthy Loddon Campaspe Place-based planning Young people Environment Landcare Roadside conservation Rural tree scheme Trees & nature strips Weeds & pests Fire, flood and emergencies Emergency Dashboard Before emergencies During emergencies After emergencies Fire and heat Floods and storms Footpaths, roads & drains Drainage Driveways Footpaths Roads Road management plan Road safety Stock on roads Street lighting Works within a road reserve Parking Parking in Echuca Parking fines Parking permits Public health Immunisations Infectious diseases Mosquitoes Nuisance and pollution complaints Safety with syringes Septic tanks Waste & recycling Bin collection services What can go in my bins? Resource Recovery Centres Waste information Victoria's Container Deposit Scheme Let's be clear on glass recycling Business Business investment Economic overview Our competitive edge Demographics Investing in the Goulburn Murray region Invest Loddon Mallee Business development Business networks Business support & promotion Business newsletter Environmental upgrade finance Goulburn Valley Designated Area Migration Agreement (GV DAMA) Business Workshops Council businesses Quarries Echuca & District Livestock Exchange Echuca Aerodrome Tools for business Starting or growing your business Starting in tourism Accommodation business Food business Health business Street furniture Recreation & events Arts & culture SPARK – arts and cultural grants Cultural groups and events Council's art collection Performing arts venues Visual arts venues Ripple Fest 2025 Creative Campaspe 2021-2031 MyCampaspe photo competition Events Event planning & permits Occupancy permits for events Events directory Flagpole program Food stalls Street stalls, raffles, collections and door-knocks Filming permit Motoring events Create an event listing Echuca Arts Precinct Council representation at your event Parks & sports facilities Pools Parks & playgrounds Recreation reserves Stadiums Outdoor pool review Parks & recreation directory Visit Campaspe Overview Visitor information Trails and maps Camping and RV services Echuca Aerodrome Library Community Facilities and Halls Plan & build Building Building permits Compliance Do I need a permit? Forms, fees & resources Owner builders Occupancy permits for events Report & consent Swimming pool & spa barriers Planning Advertised planning applications Applying for a planning permit Compliance Forms, fees & resources Heritage Native vegetation removal Planning register Planning strategies & plans Subdivisions VicSmart applications Whole farm plans Strategic planning Campaspe Planning Scheme Planning scheme amendments Growth Strategy & Township Structure Plans Works & projects Jaycee Park, Kyabram - Play Space Concept Plan Our council About council Aboriginal heritage Advocating for our community Our Councillors Australian citizenship Councillor allowances & expenses Councillor Code of Conduct Council's Management team Future Campaspe: Community Vision 2040 & Council Plan 2025-2029 Our proud past Child Safety Our commitment Report child safety concerns Reportable Conduct Scheme Resources for children, parents & carers Support services Victorian Child Safe Standards Council meetings Agendas & minutes Council meetings & dates Governance rules Live streaming Petitions & joint letters Question time Request to speak at a meeting Customer service Contact us Customer complaints Customer service requests Customer service charter Public incident report Documents Annual reports Budget, fees & charges Local laws New resident's kit Policies Strategies & plans Employment & tenders Campaspe's values Careers Tenders Volunteering Work experience and placement Governance Adjoining property details Audit & Risk Committee Charter of human rights Flag flying Freedom of information Information available to the public Instruments of delegation Privacy statement Public interest disclosures Public registers Request for compensation News & media Latest news Community newsletters Social media Echuca East Levee - Final draft ready for review Beat the heat with creative activities at Campaspe Libraries Heatwave Safety Information Now open Rochester Structure Plan Community Survey Jaycee Park, Kyabram - Play Space Concept Plan Kindergartens Youth Action Group Let's be clear on glass recycling Nominate a Veteran for Echuca War Memorial Honour Roll Campaspe Youth Awards Retirees on the River - business registration Payments & rates Rates Payments Online payment conditions Home / Our council / Employment & tenders / Careers In This Section About council Child Safety Council meetings Customer service Documents Employment & tenders Campaspe's values Careers Tenders Volunteering Work experience and placement Governance News & media Now open Payments & rates Listen Careers Current vacancies Please note: If you are experiencing issues completing your application, please contact the People and Culture team at [email protected] . Campaspe Shire Council employs more than 500 staff. We deliver more than 100 different services throughout the community including child care, waste, library, parks and gardens, local laws, infrastructure management, animal control, building and planning. The diversity of roles enable staff to access development opportunities and unique work experiences whilst enjoying the enviable lifestyle the region has to offer. The benefits of working at Council include: flexible working conditions attractive remuneration salary sacrificing options career progression opportunities through training and professional development a high regard for maintaining a healthy and safe workplace We seek to employ staff with values that are closely aligned with those of Council and who will bring their energy and talent to contribute to a dynamic and sustainable community. Find out about our Vision, Mission and Values here . How to apply To guide you through the recruitment process and to maximise your chance of your application being successful, the following steps are provided. STEP ONE: Read the position description carefully Read the position description and any other related documents to determine if you have the required skills, knowledge and experience to apply for the role. To gain a clearer understanding of the role, you are encouraged to contact the staff member named for “further information” in the position advertisement. STEP TWO: Prepare your application Your application has three parts, a cover letter, a current resume and a response to the Key Selection Criteria. A cover letter First impressions count! The cover letter introduces you. Ideally, the letter should not be more than one page and include: The title of the position you are applying for Where you saw the position advertised Why you are applying for the position Why you believe you are the right person for the job A current resume A resume is a short chronological statement of your work history and qualifications. Ideally, your resume should not exceed more than three pages and include: Your employment history (including overview of duties, employment dates, your position title and the organisation name) Your qualifications (including the qualification title, year awarded and institution name) Other information (include any key achievements, volunteer work or any other relevant information) Attach copies of your qualifications and licences, if required Include a minimum of two referees, ensuring they are contactable and are aware that we may contact them. Referees are to be someone you have reported to either currently or in the recent past. Respond to Key Selection Criteria The Key Selection Criteria (KSC) is a list of skills, attributes, knowledge and qualifications required for the position. The KSC can be found on the last page of the position description. In a separate document, write the KSC questions followed by your responses. Make sure to support your claims with evidence and examples including: Describe a situation that supports your statement. What your actions were. What you did. What the outcome of your actions was. STEP THREE: Submit your application View current vacancies here . If you require assistance with using our e-recruitment portal, please contact a member of the People and Culture team by: email: [email protected] phone: 1300 666 535 If unable to access the internet, hard copy applications may be hand delivered to a Council Service Centre, or mailed (before the closing date) to: Confidential – Campaspe Shire Council People and Culture Department PO Box 35 ECHUCA VIC 3564 What happens next? Upon receiving your application, we will: Acknowledge your application by a system generated email Please note: when submitting your application, you should receive an email within 10 minutes to confirm your email address. Please make sure to complete this step so that your application is successfully submitted. If you do not receive this email, or you are experiencing issues completing your application, please contact the People and Culture team at [email protected] . Keep your application confidential and not discuss it with anyone outside of the process Assess your application on merit Notify you of the outcome. The interview process A selection panel, usually comprised of two or three people, will interview selected applicants. The panel follows a structured process, asking all applicants the same set of questions. The questions are developed to assess how well each applicant matches the given criteria. You will also have the opportunity to ask questions throughout, and at the end, of the interview and are encouraged to think of some questions prior to interview. You are encouraged to consider some questions that may be asked and your response prior to the interview. The panel may follow up or explore particular issues that arise from individual applicants. On average an interview usually takes about 45 minutes. Candidates, who have been unsuccessful following their interview, will receive a phone call and feedback. Important Appointments may be subject to fitness for duty (also known as a pre-employment medicals), Working with Children and/or National Police Checks for specified roles as part of the recruitment process. Your application is unlikely to be short listed for consideration if the Key Selection Criteria has not been addressed. Campaspe Shire Council is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Our recruitment processes are conducted in accordance with the Equal Opportunity Act 2010. Candidates are to refrain from soliciting information outside of the recruitment process. Do not include original documents (such as qualifications) as your application will not be returned to you. If you want to apply for more than one position, please complete a separate application for each position. Referee statements will be deemed confidential information and will be classed as exempt documents under the Freedom of Information Act (1982). Positions advertised by Council attract a large number of qualified candidates. The process of reviewing applications may extend recruitment time frames. You must have a valid Australian visa with work rights and hold a valid Australian Driver’s Licence. People of Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander descent are encouraged to apply. Employment conditions are in accordance with the Campaspe Shire Council Enterprise Agreement (PDF, 2MB) . More information For questions relating to applying for a position, please contact Council on 5481 2200 and ask for a member of the People and Culture team. Back to top Contact us Campaspe Shire Council PO Box 35 Echuca VIC 3564 Phone (Free within shire only) 1300 666 535 Outside shire area 03 5481 2200 Email [email protected] National Relay Service 133 677 Customer service centres 2 Heygarth Street, Echuca 8.30am to 5.00pm More locations and opening hours Connect with us Facebook Instagram You Tube LinkedIn Zero Tolerance Statement Council is committed to creating a safe, productive, and healthy environment for all employees, contractors, volunteers, visitors, and Councillors. Council will not tolerate any form of physical, sexual, emotional, verbal, or psychological abuse, violence, harassment, intimidation, bullying, derogatory remarks, or offensive correspondence. Council acknowledges and extends its zero-tolerance stance to the families of our employees, contractors, volunteers and Councillors, ensuring their protection from any form of abuse or harassment. This includes, but is not limited to, approaching family members of Council employees, contractors, volunteers or Councillors with the intent to intimidate, harass, cause distress or attempt to influence Council matters. Acknowledgement of Country The Shire of Campaspe is the traditional lands of the Dja Dja Wurrung, Taungurung, and Yorta Yorta Peoples. We acknowledge all First Peoples and their deep and enduring connection to lands and waterways, upheld through their cultural responsibilities to Country. We pay our respect to Elders past and present for their resilience, sharing of cultural knowledge, and strength in sustaining community and Culture. With a shared commitment to mutual respect, we walk the path of reconciliation together. Disclaimer & copyright | Privacy statement | Sitemap © 2026 Campaspe Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
