About Corangamite Shire Inside Council News and Media Public Notices Have Your Say Publications Making a payment Tenders Online Contractor Safety Inductions Working for Council Current Vacancies How to Apply Why Work at Corangamite Shire? Early Years - Application Information Permits and Forms How to Apply Thank you for your interest in working at Corangamite Shire Council. We appreciate the time and effort put into every application. How long does the recruitment process usually take? The recruitment process typically takes 6 to 8 weeks, though this may vary depending on the role and the number of applications received. Will I receive confirmation that my application has been received? You will receive an email notification confirming the receipt of your application. What do I need to prepare my application? There’s no set format for your application, but to be considered for an interview, it’s important that you address the key selection criteria outlined in the position description. The following information is required as part of your application: Statements which concisely describe how you consider yourself suitable against each of the selection criteria. Wherever possible provide examples of your merit, do not simply state you meet the criteria. A succinct resume containing contact information (full name, address and daytime contact number) and a summary of your work experience. Professional referees. When preparing an application, you should: Ensure your application addresses the selection criteria. Avoid including original documents e.g.: references, certificates, as we cannot be held responsible for their return. Canvassing of Councillors or Officers will disqualify the applicant. What employee benefits are available at Corangamite Shire Council? Discover the benefits of working at Corangamite Shire here. Share Facebook X Email Print Back to top Quick Links Employment Opportunities Upcoming Events Grants & Funding Corangamite Moyne Library Service Pets & animals Rates Rubbish & Recycling Contact Us Corangamite Shire 181 Manifold Street Camperdown, Victoria, 3260 View on Map Telephone : (03) 5593 7100 Email : shire@corangamite.vic.gov.au Civic Centre opening hours : Monday to Friday, 8.30 am - 5 pm Closed on public holidays Share & Connect Like us on facebook Follow us on twitter Instagram Watch our YouTube Channel Follow us on TikTok Corangamite Shire Council acknowledges and pays our respects to the Eastern Maar and Wadawurrung peoples, as the Traditional Owners of the Lands on which we work, live and play. We also acknowledge their Elders, past and present, and recognise their ongoing cultural, spiritual and educational practices. Please note this site may contain images, voices and mentions of people who have passed. Disclaimer & Copyright | Privacy Statement | Sitemap | Acknowledgment to the Traditional Owners | A - Z Index | Child Safe Statement © 2026 Corangamite Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
