    {
      "advertised_salary_max": 36.45,
      "advertised_salary_min": 36.45,
      "advertised_salary_period": "hour",
      "advertised_salary_text": "Early Years Educators: Diploma | Greater City of Bendigo Share this job: Early Years Educators: Diploma Job No: 1550526 Location: Bendigo Employment Status: Full time, Part time & Casual, Ongoing & Temporary Closing Date: 3 Jun 2026 AEST Currently recruiting for multiple positions! Full time & Part time - ongoing/temporary and casual positions available Base hourly rate: $36.45 plus superannuation Casual hourly rate: $45.57 plus superannuation The City of Greater Bendigo is in the heart of central Victoria on Dja Dja Wurrung and Taungurung Country. Located just 90 minutes’ drive from Melbourne, our region offers all the benefits of a large city with a warm and welcoming country feel. Greater Bendigo is an attractive region that is famous for its food and wine, and boasts the Bendigo Art Gallery, theatres, stunning heritage buildings and natural surrounds that provide great recreational opportunities. There are also high quality education and health services, a wide range of housing options, excellent rail and road networks, and Bendigo Airport has regular direct QantasLink flights to Sydney. We provide more than 65 important services to support our community, which is heading towards a population of 200,000 by 2050. Now is a great time to join us! The role Do you have a passion for the education, care and supervision of children within a long day care facility and want to be part of a team that has a reputation for delivering high quality education and care programs? We currently have multiple positions available from full time, part time ongoing and temporary and casual opportunities for Early Years Educators across our friendly, intimate and established Early Learning Centres - Annie Galvin in Bendigo and Helen Jessen in Strathdale. We are looking for staff with Early Childhood Diploma qualifications who have a great skill set and looking to shape the lives of children and families every day. About You To succeed in this role, you will be committed to working in a child safe environment, be highly motivated and passionate about providing a secure, supportive environment for the needs of young children in care. You will have strong communication skills, be flexible and can work as part of a team. A satisfactory police records check, pre-employment medical check, Working with Children Check (Employee), First Aid Level 2, CPR and Anaphylaxis certifications and relevant Diploma qualifications are required for this position. Benefits Above award wages with annual pay increases, annual leave loading, paid overtime Flexible work arrangements to fit in with your needs Generous leave provisions (20 weeks paid parental leave) and learning and development opportunities. Visit our Employee Benefits website for more of our benefits. Position Description Click here to view the Position Description Click here for further information on the detailed position demands (this document provides further details on the physical and psychological requirements of the position which have been outlined in the table in the position description) Contact If you require any further information regarding this position, please contact Kristy Bennett, Coordinator Early Years Services, 03 5434 6327 . To Apply Please submit your cover letter, outlining why you are interested in this position and detailing your relevant experience with your current CV/resume by Wednesday 3 June 2026 . Apply Now Allows you to pre-fill the application using your SEEK profile information and resumé Privacy Acknowledgment The Greater Bendigo City Council (City) is a body corporate constituted as a municipal Council under the Local Government Act 2020. The City handles all personal information it collects in accordance with the Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014 (Vic) and our Privacy Policy - available here https://www.bendigo.vic.gov.au/About/Document-Library/privacy-policy-pdf. Yes I agree to the privacy statement * Personal Details * Required fi