elopment of our people, and we strive to be a workplace that is respectful, engaged, accountable, creative and honest. Are you ready to be a part of an exciting and transformative journey in the heart of one of Australia's most culturally diverse and thriving communities? Greater Dandenong City Council is an innovative and forward-thinking organisation, home to Melbourne's second-largest urban centre and a pivotal hub for manufacturing, retail and commerce in the State, Greater Dandenong boasts exceptional character and a vibrant, multicultural population that contributes to a rich cultural tapestry. About the Role Do you enjoy working outdoors and being a visible part of your Community? Council is seeking expressions of interest to work as a casual School Crossing Supervisor to assist our school students and other members of the community around schools. This role requires staff with a demonstrated ability to make responsible decisions, and an ability to relate to and communicate with young children. The position requires working casually across our Municipality (sometimes at short notice) both morning and afternoon shifts of approximately one hour per shift, on designated school days as and when required. Successful candidates must be reliable and punctual, have their own vehicle and smart phone, be well presented and able to accept responsibility for children and other pedestrians under their care when crossing busy roads around schools in all weathers. Council is committed to providing an inclusive, welcoming environment, and promoting cultural safety and wellbeing for children with zero tolerance for child abuse and harm. To Apply Applicants must adequately meet the requirements of the role contained in the position description. To view a copy of this position description, please click on the link below. School Crossing Supervisor Position Description - 247.7KB Please upload a covering letter expressing your interest in this role. You may be required to underta