      "advertised_salary_period": "hour",
      "advertised_salary_text": "Expression of Interest – Training to be a Learn to Swim Teacher - City of Greater Geelong Council Employment Opportunities Expression of Interest – Training to be a Learn to Swim Teacher Apply now Job no: 500589 Work type: Casual Classification: Band 2 Casual LSO - $43.05 p/h (inc casual loading) Categories: Swim, Sport & Leisure The role of a Learn to Swim Teacher A Learn to Swim Teacher plays an important role in creating a safe, positive and engaging environment for students of all ages and abilities. The role involves instructing and assessing participants in swimming and water safety skills through structured swim programs, while providing supervision, education and care in accordance with pool safety guidelines. Learn to Swim Teachers are responsible for building confidence in the water, giving constructive feedback to students and parents, and supporting the smooth day-to-day operation of the swim school program. They also require excellent communication and customer service skills, teamwork, professionalism, and the ability to respond calmly in emergency situations. To be eligible you must be between 16-25 years old and be able to complete 8 hours of online learning before the course date. Course dates: Course date Location Time Saturday, 13 June 2026 Geelong College 9.00-5.00 Sunday, 21 June 2026 Sunshine Leisure 9.00-5.00 Monday, 13 July 2026 Maribyrnong Aquatic Centre 9.00-5.00 If this sounds like the role for you, then click apply now! Applications and Enquiries Enquiries: Jacqueline Wurf | 5272 4979 | jwurf@geelongcity.vic.gov.au Click the Apply button to submit your application or find out more about this opportunity. If we can assist you with any reasonable adjustments in order to submit your application for this role, please contact the Talent Acquisition team via email at careers@geelongcity.vic.gov.au noting your preferred method of communication and contact details and a member of the team will be in touch. We collect demographic data to help us learn who our advertisements are reaching and how we can reach an even more diverse audience. We are committed to building a more diverse team. Your responses to our demographic questions are strictly confidential and will not be individually shared. Advertised: 25 May 2026 9:00 AM AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 02 Jun 2026 11:55 PM AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Closes Expression of Interest – Training to be a Learn to Swim Teacher 2 Jun 2026 We are seeking individuals between 16-25 years that are interested in undertaking the Lifesaving Victoria Swim teacher course. This course will be fully funded under the State Government Youth Accreditation funding grant for a limited time. Current opportunities Position Closes Expression of Interest – Training to be a Learn to Swim Teacher 2 Jun 2026 We are seeking individuals between 16-25 years that are interested in undertaking the Lifesaving Victoria Swim teacher course. This course will be fully funded under the State Government Youth Accreditation funding grant for a limited time. Talent Network Loading... Powered by PageUp How to apply Read our guide on how to apply . Applicant sign-in View the status of your application. Note: this is not your myGeelong login. Sign-in to the job portal Get regular job alerts Stay up to date about job opportunities with us. Subscribe for alerts Contact us Keep me updated We Acknowledge the Wadawurrung People as the Traditional Owners of the Land, Waterways and Skies. We pay our respects to their Elders,