te your Business Business Boost Grants Program Tenders and Suppliers Disposal of Council Assets Sale of Impounded Vehicles Plan and Build Planning Services Prepare Apply Assessment Post Assessment GreenLight Online Portal Planning Permits on Public Notice Frequently Asked Questions Planning Enforcement Glossary of Terms Building Services Building Permits Swimming Pools & Spa Registrations Building Resources and Forms Community Map Planning and Building Enquiry Wastewater and Septic Systems Contact Us Contact Council Contact a Councillor Make a Request Contact a Caravan Park Have Your Say Change My Details Media Enquiries Subscribe to E-news Community Map Home / Council / Council Resources / Plans, Strategies and Position Statements Plans, Strategies and Position Statements By Phrase or Keyword 22 Result(s) Found Council Plan The Local Government Act 2020 requires that a Community Vision and Council Plan be prepared and adopted by 31 October in the year following a general election. The Community Vision must describe the municipal community’s aspirations for the future of the municipality for a period of at least the next 10 financial years. Economic Development Strategy The Hindmarsh Shire Council Economic Development Strategy 2024-2028 builds on current economic contexts within the Hindmarsh Shire, to identify strategies and targets to support our people, employment and socio-economic wellbeing, housing, and economic output. Youth Strategy The Hindmarsh Shire Council Youth Strategy acknowledges the important role young people play in strengthening and sustaining our local community and economy. It emphasises the importance of their involvement and contributions in all aspects of community life as leaders, change makers and advocates. Sport and Recreation Strategy Sport and Recreation play a vital role in fostering healthy, connected and vibrant communities and this 10-year Sport and Recreation Strategy sets out how Council, along with local clubs, groups, and community partners, will work together to make sport and recreation more accessible, inclusive, and enjoyable for everyone. Asset Plan The Asset Plan 2025-2035 is a means of outlining the key elements involved in managing Council assets. It combines management, financial, engineering and technical practices to ensure that the level of service required by user groups is provided at the lowest long term cost to the community within the limits of any fiscal constraints that may be imposed by Council. Resource Ready Readiness Strategy The Resource Ready North-Western Victoria Energy and Mining Impact and Readiness Strategy (Strategy) provides an independent analysis of the potential impacts to our region from the capital expenditure estimated at $27.7 billion in planned transmission, renewable energy, and mining projects across nine (9) north-western Victorian local government areas. Road Management Plan The Road Management Plan describes how Hindmarsh Shire Council manages its road and related assets in accordance with the requirements of the Road Management Act 2004 (the Act), and associated Regulations and Codes of Practice. The purpose of the Road Management Plan is to establish a management system for Council to inspect, maintain and repair its public roads. Climate Adaption Strategy This document presents a refresh of Hindmarsh Shire’s Climate Adaptation Strategy by summarising recent and long-term climate trends and the accepted outlook for future climatic changes. It presents practical strategies and actions for which Council can make a meaningful contribution in offsetting potential adverse impacts from climate change and severe climate events. Domestic Animal Management Plan The Domestic Animals Act 1994 (the Act) provides the framework for Dog and Cat Management in Victoria. The Act requires all councils to develop a plan for the management of dogs and cats within its municipality. In fulfilling Council’s obligations under section 68A of the Act, the Domestic Animal Management Plan guides Council’s approach to domestic animal management over the next 4 years. Page 1 2 3 Page 1 of 3 Share Facebook Email Print Back to top Contact Us Contact Council Main Office: Address: 92 Nelson Street, NHILL VIC 3418 Phone: (03) 5391 4444 Hours: Monday to Friday - 9am to 5pm Email: info@hindmarsh.vic.gov.au Contact Hindmarsh Holiday Parks: Phone: (03) 5389 1416 Hours: Everyday 9am to 5pm Email: holidayparks@hindmarsh.vic.gov.au www.hindmarsh.vic.gov.au/holiday-parks Share and Connect Hindmarsh Shire Council Facebook Hindmarsh Shire Council Instagram Hindmarsh Shire Libraries Facebook Hindmarsh Shire Libraries Instagram Visit Hindmarsh Facebook Visit Hindmarsh Instagram Acknowledgement of Country Hindmarsh Shire Council acknowledges the Wotjobaluk, Jaadwa, Jadawadjali, Wergaia and Jupagalk Nations as Traditional Owners of Country. We recognise the important ongoing role that Indigenous people have in our community and pay our respects to their Elders, past and present. Sitemap | Disclaimer and Copyright | Privacy Statement © 2026 Hindmarsh Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
