      "advertised_salary_period": "year",
      "advertised_salary_text": "Senior Digital Delivery Lead job | Knox City Council Advertised positions Come and be part of the Knox team! Check out our currently advertised positions below. Applicant Login Create Alert All Work types Temporary Part-time All Locations Knox Civic Centre All Categories Business and Economic Development Project Delivery Reset Senior Digital Delivery Lead Apply now Job no: 496441 Work type: Temporary Part-time Location: Knox Civic Centre Categories: Business and Economic Development, Project Delivery About the role As our Senior Digital Development Lead, you will lead the redevelopment of the KnoxBiz website and the automation of the Business Permit process on behalf of the Economic Development team. The role focuses on ensuring digital solutions align with Council and Economic Development priorities, while improving customer experience and service efficiency for local businesses. Key responsibilities include engaging and managing external consultants, collaborating with key internal Council departments, and working closely with local businesses to inform the design, content and functionality of both the KnoxBiz website and the Business Permit process. This is a part time temporary specialist role based at Knox City Council in Wantirna South. We support flexible working arrangements while ensuring operational needs of the role are met. This is a Band 7 classified role. Remuneration will be $110,732.77 (pro rata for part-time), plus superannuation in accordance with the Superannuation Guarantee. What you will bring to this role The key selection criteria for this role are: Demonstrated experience leading the delivery of complex digital projects, including website redevelopment and digital service automation, within a public sector or similar organisational context. Demonstrated experience in procuring, managing and coordinating external consultants and contractors to deliver high-quality digital outcomes within agreed timeframes and budgets. Strong stakeholder engagement skills, with excellent interpersonal and communication abilities. Knowledge of procurement and governance requirements, including demonstrated experience managing short-term contracts within a local government or public sector context. Competence in Microsoft Office applications such as Outlook, Word and PowerPoint; knowledge of ePathway or similar systems used in local government is desirable. A degree or tertiary qualification in digital, communications, business, project management, information technology or a related field, combined with relevant experience. How to apply Please submit your application, including your resume and cover letter online via the ‘Apply’ button by 11.45pm on Thursday 4 June 2026. All applications must be made via the online portal. No applications direct to the hiring manager will be considered. For further information on this role please contact Michelle Bishop, Head of Economic Development, at michelle.bishop@knox.vic.gov.au or on 9738 9705. A link to the position description can be found in the job listing on our Knox City Council Jobs and Careers page. Please note: Candidates will be shortlisted as applications are received and this role may close earlier than the anticipated closing date. Why work at Knox Discover your future at Knox City Council, where you will deliver meaningful impact, find great opportunities and work with committed people to shape our community. As an employee of Knox, you can enjoy: Accrued or rostered days off available for full-time roles, depending on operational requirements Broad range of leave options including up to 16 weeks primary and up to 4 weeks secondary parental leave Salary sacrifice option for Council-owned childcare fees Opportunities to take on temporary roles or work in different teams to build skills and support career growth Support towards further study 50% off Knox Leisureworks memberships Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for support in managing personal and work-related challenges. To find out more about the benefits of working at Knox City Council, visit knox.vic.gov.au/why-work-knox Inherent requirements To view the inherent requirements for this position please see attachment below. Office Based role(s) - Inherent Requirements Table .DOCX Our commitments Knox City Council is an Equal Opportunity Employer that is committed to providing a workplace that embraces diversity and inclusion. We are committed to a positive, barrier-free recruitment process. If you have any support or access requirements, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Knox City Council has zero tolerance for child abuse and all forms of harm to children. All children and young people who access our services, programs, events and facilities have the right to feel safe and be safe. This includes spaces owned or managed by Council. We take the wellbeing and safety of children and young people in our care seriously. We maintain a child safe organisation by embedding the protection of children into everyday thinking and practice. All Knox City Council employees, contractors and volunteers are responsible for ensuring children and young people are valued, heard and protected from abuse. Knox City Council acknowledges our offices are located on the traditional lands of the Wurundjeri Woi-wurrung and Bunurong people of the Kulin Nation. Follow us For more information about Knox City Council and to stay up to date, follow us on LinkedIn . Position Description Advertised: 21 May 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 04 Jun 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Senior Digital Delivery Lead Location: Knox Civic Centre Location: 4 Jun 2026 We have an exciting opportunity for a Senior Digital Development Lead to join our Economic Development team until 31 March 2027. View Job Listing 0 Opportunities Senior Digital Delivery Lead Location: Knox Civic Centre Close Date: 4 Jun 2026 We have an exciting opportunity for a Senior Digital Development Lead to join our Economic Development team until 31 March 2027. View Job Expression of Interest Loading... Powered by PageUp Why us? People are our community inside and out. They are who we serve, who we are and at the heart of everything we do and believe in. We will be defined by our resilient, diverse and capable team. Knox will support you to keep growing and leveraging your passions, talents and skills to achieve amazing results for our community. Sitemap Accessibility Contact Council Disclaimer Privacy Copyright © Knox City Council ABN: 24 477 480 661 Knox City Council acknowledges the traditional custodians of the City of Knox, the Wurundjeri and Bunurong people of the Kulin Nation.",
