ouncillors Councillor Steve Rabie (Mayor) Councillor James Tehan (Deputy Mayor) Councillor Mandy Treasure Councillor Bonnie Clark Councillor Tim Berenyi Elections Elections Voting Entitlements Election campaign donation return Governance & Public Transparency Child Safe Statement of Commitment Customer Service Commitment Councillor Code of Conduct Freedom of Information Personal Interest Returns Public Information Public Interest Disclosure Register of Delegations and Authorisations Gender Equality Action Plan Petitions Australia Day, Awards & Citizenship Ceremonies Work With Us Career & Job Opportunities Information for Applicants Plans, Strategies & Policies Document Listing Key Strategic Documents Public Notices Advocacy Planning Search Home / Council / Work With Us / Career & Job Opportunities / Community Resilience Officer Community Resilience Officer Applications closing on 15 June 2026, 05:00 PM Reference number 41.2 Job Type Fixed Term, Full Time Package Remuneration will be based on Band 5 Level A classification $76,917.88 per annum ($38.9261 per hour), plus superannuation Position Description Position-Description-Community-Resilience-Officer-March-2026.pdf (PDF, 1MB) Mansfield Shire Council is looking for an enthusiastic, experienced and community focused individual to take up the role of Community Resilience Officer. The successful candidate will assist with the coordination of planning, implementation and ongoing review of Council’s emergency management responsibilities in accordance with the Emergency Management Act and State Emergency Management Plan and Municipal Emergency Management Plan. Reporting to the Manager Bushfire Recovery, the role also includes responsibility for provides support to the Municipal Emergency Management Officer (MEMO) and Municipal Recovery Manager (MRM) and the Municipal Emergency Management Planning committee (MEMPC) with the delivery of their legislated roles and responsibilities, in relations to the AGRN 1242. Remuneration will be based on Band 5 Level A classification $76,917.88 per annum ($38.9261 per hour), plus superannuation according to the Mansfield Shire Council Enterprise Agreement 2024. Applications close at 5.00pm on Monday 15 June 2026. This is a Fixed Term, Full Time role until 30 June 2028. For more information about this role please refer to the position description and the Information for Applicants page of Council's website here . For a confidential discussion regarding the position please contact Tamara Watson, Manager Bushfire Recovery on 0438 823 475. Apply Now (PDF, 823KB) Share this job by email How to Apply All applications must contain: a covering letter the completed Employment Application Form an up to date Resume, and a document addressing the Key Selection Criteria More Information Related Information About Council Organisational Structure Share Facebook Email Print LinkedIn X Back to top Quick Links Mansfield Library Mansfield Swimming Pool Cemeteries Engage with us Our Tourism Website State Government Coronavirus Support Contact Us Address 33 Highett Street Mansfield VIC 3722 View on Map Opening Hours Monday to Friday 8.30 am to 4.30 pm Email: council@mansfield.vic.gov.au Telephone: 03 5775 8555 ABN 74 566 834 923 Contact Us Connect & Share Like us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Watch our YouTube Channel Follow us on LinkedIn Our Commitment We are committed to child safety , our customers , gender equality , accessibility and climate action . Acknowledgement of Country Mansfield Shire Council acknowledges the Taungurung people as the traditional custodians and we pay our respects to their Elders past and present. Council extends that respect to all members of our community. Disclaimer | Privacy | Sitemap © 2026 Mansfield Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
