il Meeting Council Committees Councillors Councillor Steve Rabie (Mayor) Councillor James Tehan (Deputy Mayor) Councillor Mandy Treasure Councillor Bonnie Clark Councillor Tim Berenyi Elections Elections Voting Entitlements Election campaign donation return Governance & Public Transparency Child Safe Statement of Commitment Customer Service Commitment Councillor Code of Conduct Freedom of Information Personal Interest Returns Public Information Public Interest Disclosure Register of Delegations and Authorisations Gender Equality Action Plan Petitions Australia Day, Awards & Citizenship Ceremonies Work With Us Career & Job Opportunities Information for Applicants Plans, Strategies & Policies Document Listing Key Strategic Documents Public Notices Advocacy Planning Search Home / Council / Work With Us / Career & Job Opportunities / Program Manager CODI (Collaborative Digital Transformation) Program Manager CODI (Collaborative Digital Transformation) Applications closing on 08 June 2026, 05:00 PM Reference number 12.2 Job Type Fixed Term, Part / Full Time Package Remuneration will be based on $136,405.28 annually ($69.03 per hour) or pro rata amount for part time, plus superannuation Position Description Position-Description-Program-Manager-CODI-May-2026.pdf (PDF, 2MB) CODI is a joint initiative between Benalla, Mansfield, Murrindindi and Strathbogie councils to modernise and improve council services digitally. We are looking for an enthusiastic, experienced and community focused individual to take up the position of Program Manager CODI. The successful candidate will be responsible for overseeing stakeholder management, governance and strategic direction of the CODI program. Reporting to the General Manager Investment & Planning, the role primarily focuses on ongoing strategic reporting to the Program Control Group (PCG) and Program Steering Group (PSG), contract and vendor management, coordination of key stakeholders, procurement of future program scope or enhancements and identifying strategic opportunities to maximise value for all member Councils. This is a Fixed Term, Part- or Full-Time position till 30 June 2028. Remuneration will be based on $136,405.28 annually ($69.03 per hour) or pro rata amount for part time, plus superannuation according to the Mansfield Shire Council Enterprise Agreement 2024. Applications close at 5.00pm on Monday 8 June 2026. For more information about this role please refer to the position description and the Information for Applicants page of Council's website here . For a confidential discussion regarding the position please contact Melissa Crane, General Manager Investment and Planning on (03) 5775 8548. Apply Now (PDF, 823KB) Share this job by email How to Apply All applications must contain: a covering letter the completed Employment Application Form an up to date Resume, and a document addressing the Key Selection Criteria More Information Related Information About Council Organisational Structure Share Facebook Email Print LinkedIn X Back to top Quick Links Mansfield Library Mansfield Swimming Pool Cemeteries Engage with us Our Tourism Website State Government Coronavirus Support Contact Us Address 33 Highett Street Mansfield VIC 3722 View on Map Opening Hours Monday to Friday 8.30 am to 4.30 pm Email: council@mansfield.vic.gov.au Telephone: 03 5775 8555 ABN 74 566 834 923 Contact Us Connect & Share Like us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Watch our YouTube Channel Follow us on LinkedIn Our Commitment We are committed to child safety , our customers , gender equality , accessibility and climate action . Acknowledgement of Country Mansfield Shire Council acknowledges the Taungurung people as the traditional custodians and we pay our respects to their Elders past and present. Council extends that respect to all members of our community. Disclaimer | Privacy | Sitemap © 2026 Mansfield Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
