ies: Before, During and After Extreme heat and heat health Council advocacy Advocacy Priorities Submissions on key issues Advocacy Partnerships Council service finder Our sites: Active Merri-bek Conversations Merri-bek Love Merri-bek, Buy Local Zero Carbon Merri-bek Alerts Merri-bek City Council is committed to being a Child Safe organisation and has zero tolerance for child abuse. Clear alerts Work experience Home My Council Careers at Merri-bek Work experience On this page: We provide work experience opportunities for local students and disadvantaged community members. Work experience opportunities We offer three types of work experience: Formal work experience as part of an education course (secondary or tertiary students) Community-based work experience through an organisation that works with disadvantaged community member Non-structured work experience that is not required as part of a course. Request a work experience placement Merri-bek is partnering with the Inner Northern Local Learning and Employment Network (INLLEN) to coordinate work experience placements. INLLEN works with local schools, students and host organisations across Merri-bek, Darebin and Yarra to ensure placements are well-prepared, safe and meaningful. Year 10 high school work experience enquiries Contact: Inner Northern LLEN (INLLEN) Kristyn Martin – kmartin@inllen.org.au www.inllen.org.au Year 11, 12 high school and tertiary work placement enquiries To apply for a work placement with Merri-bek, complete the Work Experience Request Form (DOCX 111Kb) For general work placements, send your completed application to work.experience@merri-bek.vic.gov.au . For work placements with Merri-bek Libraries , send your completed application to libraryplacements@merri-bek.vic.gov.au Once you have submitted our application, your request is sent to the manager of the relevant area. If the request can be accommodated, we will provide you with the manager's contact details. It is then your responsibility to contact the manager to discuss further arrangements. We recommended looking for work experience elsewhere if you do not hear back from us within two weeks. For more work experience information visit the Department of Education and Training website. Traineeships We work with AGA Apprenticeships Plus to provide traineeship opportunities. Traineeships can be: undertaken on a full-time or part-time basis used as a stepping stone to start or further a career in an industry paid opportunities to combine formal learning (e.g. TAFE) with workplace training. To find out more about traineeships at Merri-bek City Council visit AGA Apprenticeships Plus or call 1800 818 105 . Explore this section Explore this section My Council About Council Councillors Mayor and Councillors Councillor conduct Council elections CEO and executive team Renaming Merri-bek Sister cities and friendship cities Our sustainability story Council budget Advisory committees Council Plan and Community Vision Governance rules Council and committee meetings Council meetings Council meeting dates, locations and questions Next Council meeting agenda Council meeting minutes and past agendas Planning and Related Matters meetings Planning and Related Matters meetings, dates and locations Next Planning and Related Matters meeting agenda Planning and Related Matters meeting minutes and past agendas Advisory Committees Audit and Risk Committee Children's Reference Group Environmental Sustainability and Climate Resilience Advisory Committee Friends of Aileu Community Committee Gender Equality Reference Group Health, Wellbeing and Social Inclusion Advisory Committee LGBTIQA+ Reference Group Liveability Advisory Committee Merri-bek Arts Advisory Committee Older Persons Reference Group Past Advisory Committees and Reference Groups Strategic Transport Reference Group External committees Livestreaming Engage Conversations Merri-bek Petitions Committees Social media user guidelines Careers at Merri-bek Current vacancies App