 Before, During and After Extreme heat and heat health Council advocacy Advocacy Priorities Submissions on key issues Advocacy Partnerships Council service finder Our sites: Active Merri-bek Conversations Merri-bek Love Merri-bek, Buy Local Zero Carbon Merri-bek Alerts Merri-bek City Council is committed to being a Child Safe organisation and has zero tolerance for child abuse. Clear alerts First Peoples Careers Home My Council Careers at Merri-bek First Peoples Careers On this page: First Peoples Employment Plan The First Peoples Employment Plan 2025-2028 has been developed through the extensive review of the inaugural First Peoples Employment Plan 2022-2025. To develop our First Peoples Employment Plan, Merri-bek City Council worked in consultation with: Wurundjeri Woi-wurrung Cultural Heritage Aboriginal Corporation Merri-bek’s First Peoples Advisory Committee Merri-bek’s First Peoples staff Merri-bek's leadership teams. Merri-bek City Council’s vision “Our vision is that Merri-bek City Council is an employer of choice by First Peoples. Our workplace and practices are culturally safe and supportive of First Peoples expressions of identity, gender, cultural values and practices, abilities, socio-economic status and rights to self-determination. We provide opportunities at all organisational levels, that realise First Peoples staff career objectives and aspirations as consistent with our Statement of Commitment to First Peoples .” Benefits of working at Merri-bek Support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff includes: Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff network ongoing professional development opportunities tailored cultural support and opportunity to engage in cultural wellbeing workshops Cultural Connection space for staff access to culturally safe employee support and cultural leave. Learn more about our values, staff benefits and why Merri-bek is a great place to work . Positions available Find out which job opportunities are available on our Current Vacancies page. Don’t worry if you don’t see a current First Peoples identified role, we encourage First Peoples to apply for any of our positions across Council. Work experience and traineeships Find work experience opportunities, request a work experience placement and learn about traineeships on our Work Experience page. Register your interest If you cannot see a current role that interests you, please complete our First Peoples Careers expression of interest form . Applying for a job at Merri-bek Our Applying for a job page provides useful information including: how to apply writing a resume responding to key selection criteria. We also provide support with the application process - see our contact details. Contact First Peoples Careers For more information or support, please reach out to First Peoples Careers – firstpeoplescareers@merri-bek.vic.gov.au Explore this section Explore this section My Council About Council Councillors Mayor and Councillors Councillor conduct Council elections CEO and executive team Renaming Merri-bek Sister cities and friendship cities Our sustainability story Council budget Advisory committees Council Plan and Community Vision Governance rules Council and committee meetings Council meetings Council meeting dates, locations and questions Next Council meeting agenda Council meeting minutes and past agendas Planning and Related Matters meetings Planning and Related Matters meetings, dates and locations Next Planning and Related Matters meeting agenda Planning and Related Matters meeting minutes and past agendas Advisory Committees Audit and Risk Committee Children's Reference Group Environmental Sustainability and Climate Resilience Advisory Committee Friends of Aileu Community Committee Gender Equality Reference Group Health, Wellbeing and Social Inclusion Advisory Committee LGBTIQA+ Reference Group Liveability Advisory Committee Merri-bek Arts Advisory Committee Older Persons Reference Group Past Advisory Committees and Refer