accessible resources, insights and tools for business decision-making Deliver early-stage business support programs Foster a collaborative, business-friendly culture across Council About you You are a proactive and customer-focused professional who thrives in complex environments and is passionate about supporting business and delivering positive local economic outcomes. Experience in economic development or business-facing regulatory environments, ideally within local government. This role is suited to both economic development professionals or candidates with experience in one or more of the following areas - Planning, Building, Environmental Health or Community Laws. Strong understanding of regulatory frameworks and how they apply to business establishment and growth Ability to translate complex information into clear, practical and accessible advice Proven project management, analytical and reporting skills Confidence working across multidisciplinary teams and coordinating stakeholders to deliver outcomes A customer-focused mindset with the ability to build trust and strong relationships Experience identifying and implementing process or system improvements Highly developed communication and facilitation skills, including workshops and business engagement Strong organisational skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and work autonomously If you’re excited about this role but your experience doesn’t perfectly match every criteria, we encourage you to apply—we value diverse perspectives and transferable skills. Benefits City of Monash is a dynamic organisation committed to providing excellence in service delivery. Located in the eastern region, Monash is a cosmopolitan and culturally diverse city, close to the demographic centre of Melbourne. As a City of Monash employee, your personal and professional development is a key focus for us. You will have access to: Supportive and experienced leaders that care for your development and wellbeing Vibrant 