 on creating pathways for our people to enable them to be their very best, in an environment that places flexibility as the cornerstone of our people strategy. We are constantly growing and evolving in a working environment where progression and innovation is a must; we support our people to do things differently, to challenge the way things have ‘always been done’ and to create something unique. We support this by employing a 'yes first' mantra then working together to establish a means in which to achieve. We commit to listening to our people and generating positive change based on this feedback. The ongoing development of our people is also at the forefront so the provision of training and development across multiple platforms enables us to create our next team of superstars across Council. Moorabool Shire Council provides industry leading conditions of employment. Here’s a few just to whet your appetite! Additional annual leave - top of band after 12 months Up to two additional annual leave days depending on leave accruals Access to three health and wellbeing days over the life of the Health and Wellbeing Strategy Additional carers leave of two days per year, non cumulative 38 hours of IVF leave Payment of increments whilst on parental leave Six months of super paid on unpaid parental leave Provision of training days whilst on parental leave Parental leave available after the probationary period (6 months) One week addition to both primary (19) and secondary (3) carers leave Combine and split leave entitlements if both parents work at Moorabool Flexibility Spread of Hours Clause instigated by the employee Mental Health Awareness Training & Contact Officers Updates to the Discretionary Leave Clause (now includes gender affirmation related activities, natural disaster and foster caring) Engineer’s Allowance update. Together with our people, we are on a journey to innovate and create, and to deliver exceptional customer service for our community. So, if you want to experience all that Moorabool has to offer and make a real difference, come and join the team and be part of the journey. Was this page helpful? * (required) Help us improve this site Yes Maybe No How can we improve this page? Email address * (required) Type the characters you see in the image below * (Required) Generate new image Read aloud Please enter the text in the image Back to top Contact us Moorabool Shire Council Principal office 15 Stead Street Ballan Victoria 3342 T (03) 5366 7100 E info@moorabool.vic.gov.au Connect and follow Like us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Follow us on LinkedIn Download our app Watch our YouTube channel Follow our other social media Acknowledgement of Country Council respectfully acknowledges the Traditional Owners of the land which includes the Wurundjeri Woi Wurrung, Wadawurrung and Dja Dja Wurrung people. We pay our respects to the Elders past, present and emerging. Disclaimer, accessibility and copyright | Privacy statement | Child Safe Statement of Commitment © 2026 Moorabool Shire Council | Powered by Granicus ×",
