nspections Construction Management Plan (CMP) Road Openings / Drainage Connections - FAQs Vehicle Access to Shire Reserves Vehicle Crossing / Crossover - FAQs Heritage Aboriginal Cultural Heritage Assistance to Heritage Place Owners Heritage Awards Heritage Grants Heritage Places Since European Settlement Heritage Overlay and Planning Permits Heritage Studies Conservation Management Plans Ranelagh Estate Mount Eliza Municipal Heritage Review Heritage Places Policy Contact Us Report a problem Report a stormwater drainage issue Report a road maintenance issue Report a tree concern Report a street lighting fault Report dumped waste or rubbish Report a litter or public street bin issue Report a concern with a Shire building Report a concern with a short stay rental property Report a parking concern Report a sign concern Report other concerns Report a road safety issue Request a review of parking restrictions Report a footpath problem Report a noise or general nuisance issue Abandoned trolleys Ask a Question Online Payments and Services Complaints Be scam savvy Customer Charter Home / About Us / Careers & Volunteering / Become a Shire Volunteer Become a Shire Volunteer Learn more about what's involved in volunteering with the Mornington Peninsula Shire and the kinds of roles available. Volunteering as a Shire Volunteer can provide you with an opportunity to do something positive for your local community. Why Volunteer? Volunteering offers numerous benefits, such as: Making a positive impact on your community Building connections and forming new relationships Developing new skills and gaining valuable experience Boosting your mental and physical well-being Increasing your sense of purpose and fulfillment Enhancing your resume and career prospects Overall, volunteering can be a rewarding and enriching experience for both the volunteer and the community. Our Volunteer Programs Meals on Wheels volunteers Volunteers help the community's most vulnerable with delivery of healthy meals and to stay connected to their community. The Briars at Mount Martha A range of opportunities are available at the Briars for those passionate about local history, wildlife and agriculture. Community Houses Community Houses welcome people from all walks of life, creating opportunities for individuals and groups to enrich their lives through connections they might not otherwise make. Home Library Service Our Libraries provide free monthly deliveries of library materials to housebound residents through its Home Library Service. Shire Nursery Our Nursery welcomes volunteers with an interest in growing plants and gardening. Mornington Peninsula Regional Gallery Experience the Mornington Peninsula Regional Gallery from the inside by assisting with front of house, being an exhibition attendant or a gallery guide. Mornington Peninsula Visitor Information Centre Volunteers play a key role in promoting tourism experiences to visitors and local residents. TAC L2P Program A program to help learner drivers complete their on-road driving experience and gain confidence on the road. Mount Martha Historical House Safeguard and conserve the history and heritage of Mount Martha House and its community, ensuring its accessibility to all. Committees Be part of a committee or local management support group. FAQs Visit a list of Frequently Asked Questions around volunteering. Eco Living Garden Volunteers If you’re a keen gardener or if you just like working outdoors with others, we’d love to have you join our small group of volunteers in our unique display garden. Eco Living Display Centre Guide If you’re interested in sustainable design, you can join our team of tour guides for the Eco Living Display Centre. Eco Living Harvest Exchange stall host Join our friendly community of home gardeners and occasionally host the harvest exchange at the Eco Centre. Gardens for Wildlife Garden Guide Inspire residents to create wildlife friendly gardens by providing home visits, tailored advice, & follow-up recommendations to help protect our local plants and animals. Rosebud Library Volunteers We are looking for Library Volunteers to help at our Rosebud library. Volunteering Mornington Peninsula We recruit volunteers throughout the year and advertise roles through our volunteering page . Volunteering Mornington Peninsula provides an opportunity for community organisations to list their current volunteering vacancies and for volunteers to search a database of volunteering opportunities for one that meets their skills, experience and interests. Back to top Contact Us Mornington Peninsula Shire Private Bag 1000 Rosebud, Victoria, 3939 Email: customerservice@mornpen.vic.gov.au Phone: 1300 850 600 Service centre and connection point operating hours and days vary by location. Service Centres Rosebud Office 90 Besgrove Street, Rosebud Mornington Office 2 Queen Street, Mornington Hastings Office 21 Marine Parade, Hastings Connection Points Somerville 1085 Frankston-Flinders Road, Somerville Dromana 359B Point Nepean Road, Dromana Red Hill 137 Shoreham Road, Red Hill Sorrento 860–868 Melbourne Road, Sorrento Visit our Other Sites MP Regional Gallery Our Library Mount Martha Public Golf Course MP Business Arts and Culture Volunteering Mornington Peninsula Share & Connect Like us on Facebook Check out our Instagram Watch our YouTube videos Sign-up to our email bulletins Acknowledgement Mornington Peninsula Shire acknowledges and pays respect to the Bunurong people, the Traditional Custodians of these lands and waters. We welcome and include Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, LGBTIQA+, and multicultural community members of all ages and abilities. Disclaimer and Copyright | Privacy Statement | Terms and Conditions | Accessibility © 2026 Mornington Peninsula Shire | Powered by Granicus",
