onstruction Management Plan (CMP) Road Openings / Drainage Connections - FAQs Vehicle Access to Shire Reserves Vehicle Crossing / Crossover - FAQs Heritage Aboriginal Cultural Heritage Assistance to Heritage Place Owners Heritage Awards Heritage Grants Heritage Places Since European Settlement Heritage Overlay and Planning Permits Heritage Studies Conservation Management Plans Ranelagh Estate Mount Eliza Municipal Heritage Review Heritage Places Policy Contact Us Report a problem Report a stormwater drainage issue Report a road maintenance issue Report a tree concern Report a street lighting fault Report dumped waste or rubbish Report a litter or public street bin issue Report a concern with a Shire building Report a concern with a short stay rental property Report a parking concern Report a sign concern Report other concerns Report a road safety issue Request a review of parking restrictions Report a footpath problem Report a noise or general nuisance issue Abandoned trolleys Ask a Question Online Payments and Services Complaints Be scam savvy Customer Charter Home / About Us / Careers & Volunteering / Traineeships Traineeships Work. Learn. Grow. Be paid while you work and study. Earn a Certificate IV in Business. Recruitment for the Traineeship Program is currently closed. To be notified of the next intake, please complete our form below. Submit your expression of interest Are you looking to gain practical on-the-job work experience and a qualification? The Shire is offering you the chance to improve lives and shape your own career in a truly special place. We are currently recruiting for both Business Trainee and Identified Business Trainee positions. If you identify as a First Nations person, we encourage you to apply for the Identified Business Trainee role. You’ll enjoy diverse work and opportunities to grow, working in a truly special community and a region of outstanding natural beauty. In return for your passion and commitment to moving the Shire forward, we offer great benefits and the balance you need to bring the best you. As a trainee, you’ll work at the Shire for a 12-month program which will offer learning and development opportunities, the chance to expand personal and professional capabilities, while completing a Certificate IV in Business - a formal and recognised qualification, through a Registered Training Organisation. The Shire’s Traineeship Program provides flexible employment and training opportunities for people wanting to build a career. The program is aimed at attracting: School leavers Adults entering or returning to the workforce, reskilling, or seeking a career change. To hear insights from our previous trainees, please watch this video: What should you expect? The 12-month Traineeship Program is a full-time position. Participants in the program are supported every step of the way with opportunities to learn and grow on the job while completing a Certificate IV in Business - a formal and recognised qualification. Huge Opportunities Benefit from the wide and varied work that the Shire offers making it easier for you to find your perfect fit. Support & Guidance Trainees receive a circle of support that includes your Program facilitator, supervisor, mentor, study provider and the Australian Apprenticeship Support Network. Diversity & Inclusion We celebrate an inclusive workplace culture that promotes and values diversity. Our employees feel empowered to share their experiences and ideas. Skills for your Future Gain a nationally recognised Certificate IV in Business qualification by combining employment (real wages) and training (formal study). Make a Difference Spend your working hours doing something that makes your local community a better place to be. Health & Wellbeing We are committed to providing and maintaining a safe and healthy work environment with programs that seek to optimise the health and well-being of its employees. Who are we looking for? If you are looking to kickstart your career, a career change, to re-enter the workforce, the Mornington Peninsula Shire Traineeship Program is a great opportunity to take you in a new direction. Don’t worry if you don’t have experience, our Values are everything - Integrity, Courage, Openness, Respect & Excellence. If these resonate with you, what are you waiting for? We want team orientated individuals who are willing to go above and beyond. You must be reliable, punctual, and willing to follow instructions. We celebrate an inclusive workplace culture that promotes and values diversity. Our employees feel empowered to share their experiences and ideas. At the Shire, we see all forms of diversity as real value for the region and a reflection of our community. Take this opportunity to kick start your career and earn while you learn! Is Council right for you? Our Core Values set the framework for how we work together to achieve outstanding outcomes for our customers and our community. Our values guide us in clearly defining and communicating: How we do things at the Shire; How we make decisions in the best interests of the community we serve; and How we hold ourselves and each other accountable the highest standards of performance and conduct. Our Values set our organisational culture and articulate the shared behaviours we are all required to live by when making decisions in the course of our work. In living our values, we build a collective culture committed to high performance, and send a clear message to our colleagues and our community about how we go about our business. Visit: Our Organisational Values page. What kind of work could I do? Your Career. Your Community. The scale and diversity of the work we do means the Shire can offer you many different career paths. Some examples are: Business Services Communications Community Services Customer Service Economic Development Engineering & Asset Management Environment Finance Governance Human Resources Information Technology Park & Sports facilities Planning & Development Procurement Property Tourism, Culture & Recreation Eligibility criteria To be eligible for a traineeship, applicants must: Be aged 18 years or older and no longer at school. Be able to meet citizen, residency, and visa requirements to undertake a traineeship. Not have already completed a Certificate IV (or higher) qualification in Business or a similar field. Application process Stage 1 Applications Online Applications open Online Applications close 20 October 2025 9 November 2025 Stage 2 Application Shortlisting Shortlisting of applications received 9 -18 November Stage 3 Assessment Centre Interview and Group Activities (2-hour commitment) 18 and 20 November 2025 Stage 4 Online Assessment Testing language, literacy and numeracy skills December 2025 Stage 5 Reference and Background Checks Reference checks from two referees provided by you. A criminal history check and Working with Children Check is also required prior to an offer of employment. December 2025 Stage 6 Offer A verbal offer will be made, followed by a letter of offer and new starter information. December 2025 Stage 7 Commencement Monday 2 February 2026 Frequently Asked Questions Is it possible to get a copy of the handouts from the information session? Yes. Please email employment.pathways@mornpen.vic.gov.au to receive a copy. I did not attend the information session, will it affect my chances of being considered for the role? Missing the Information session will not affect your ability to apply. Applications open on 20 October and our accepted through our Current Vacancies page. Is there a minimum or maximum age limit? The Traineeship Program is open to anyone aged 18 and over. We welcome applications from adults of all ages. I have recently completed a degree, is this pathway right for me? The Traineeship Program provides the opportunity to gain a Certificate IV in Business and is ideal if you are looking to explore a new career path. If your goal is to use your degree specifically within local government, we recommend keeping an eye on our Current Vacancies page for roles that align with your qualifications. I have recently completed a Diploma in Business, can I apply? Unfortunately, if you have already completed a higher-level qualification in the same field, we are unable to accept your application. Was this page helpful? * (required) Help us improve this site Yes No Please tell us why: If you have a general enquiry or want to make a complaint, contact us . Type the characters you see in the image below * (Required) Generate new image Read aloud Please enter the text in the image Back to top Contact Us Mornington Peninsula Shire Private Bag 1000 Rosebud, Victoria, 3939 Email: customerservice@mornpen.vic.gov.au Phone: 1300 850 600 Service centre and connection point operating hours and days vary by location. Service Centres Rosebud Office 90 Besgrove Street, Rosebud Mornington Office 2 Queen Street, Mornington Hastings Office 21 Marine Parade, Hastings Connection Points Somerville 1085 Frankston-Flinders Road, Somerville Dromana 359B Point Nepean Road, Dromana Red Hill 137 Shoreham Road, Red Hill Sorrento 860–868 Melbourne Road, Sorrento Visit our Other Sites MP Regional Gallery Our Library Mount Martha Public Golf Course MP Business Arts and Culture Volunteering Mornington Peninsula Share & Connect Like us on Facebook Check out our Instagram Watch our YouTube videos Sign-up to our email bulletins Acknowledgement Mornington Peninsula Shire acknowledges and pays respect to the Bunurong people, the Traditional Custodians of these lands and waters. We welcome and include Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, LGBTIQA+, and multicultural community members of all ages and abilities. Disclaimer and Copyright | Privacy Statement | Terms and Conditions | Accessibility © 2026 Mornington Peninsula Shire | Powered by Granicus",
