 requirements. Work experience placements are open to all students living or attending a high school in the Mornington Peninsula region. Applying for work experience Please fill in the Work Experience Expression of Interest Form below and include reasons for wanting to undertake a placement at the Shire. While the Shire will make every effort to offer work experience placements, at peak times of the year we may not be able to accommodate all students. Apply for a work experience placement Was this page helpful? * (required) Help us improve this site Yes No Please tell us why: If you have a general enquiry or want to make a complaint, contact us . Type the characters you see in the image below * (Required) Generate new image Read aloud Please enter the text in the image Back to top Contact Us Mornington Peninsula Shire Private Bag 1000 Rosebud, Victoria, 3939 Email: customerservice@mornpen.vic.gov.au Phone: 1300 850 600 Service centre and connection point operating hours and days vary by location. Service Centres Rosebud Office 90 Besgrove Street, Rosebud Mornington Office 2 Queen Street, Mornington Hastings Office 21 Marine Parade, Hastings Connection Points Somerville 1085 Frankston-Flinders Road, Somerville Dromana 359B Point Nepean Road, Dromana Red Hill 137 Shoreham Road, Red Hill Sorrento 860–868 Melbourne Road, Sorrento Visit our Other Sites MP Regional Gallery Our Library Mount Martha Public Golf Course MP Business Arts and Culture Volunteering Mornington Peninsula Share & Connect Like us on Facebook Check out our Instagram Watch our YouTube videos Sign-up to our email bulletins Acknowledgement Mornington Peninsula Shire acknowledges and pays respect to the Bunurong people, the Traditional Custodians of these lands and waters. We welcome and include Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, LGBTIQA+, and multicultural community members of all ages and abilities. Disclaimer and Copyright | Privacy Statement | Terms and Conditions | Accessibility © 2026 Mornington