rmit Works on Council land permit Asset protection permit Residential parking permit Accessible parking permit Planning permit Busking permit Open air burn permit Excess animals permit Mobile food business (on Council land) permit Road closure for events permit Community event signage permit Event registration Amend a planning permit Extension of time to a planning permit Siting variation consent application Projections beyond the street alignment consent application Build on flood-prone land consent application Building demolition consent application Building permit Swimming pool or spa registration Certificate of Barrier Compliance Places of public entertainment permit (POPE) Temporary structures permit Fundraising Collecting charitable money or gifts permit Camping on public or private land VicSmart Planning Permit Home / Council / Work with us / Current vacancies / Direct Care Worker Direct Care Worker Ongoing Applications Reference number 23-DCW Job Type Part Time or Casual Package Band 2 Position Description Position-Description-Direct-Care-Worker-Part-Time-or-Casual.pdf (PDF, 182KB) Part Time or Casual positions Ongoing Band 2 Part time - commencing $61,425 pa (pro-rata) / $31.09 per hour + Super + Allowances Casual - $38.86 per hour (incl. loading) + Super + Allowances Closing Date: Applications are accepted at all times. We are seeking skilled and experienced professional care workers who love supporting people to live independently in the community. We currently provide services in Mount Alexander Shire and Central Goldfields Shire. This is your opportunity to bring your passion and skills to be part of a professional and dedicated team providing high quality in-home support to frail older people and people with disabilities in our community. The role provides tailored services to help clients live healthy, independent and active lives through assistance with daily tasks and activities. If you have any queries or would like to discuss the role, the key contact is: Sarah Newstead In Home Support Coordinator (03) 5471 1845 Please note these positions require staff to be triple vaccinated (2 doses plus a booster). To apply, please provide a cover letter (no more than 2 pages) outlining why you are interested and the best candidate for this role, and your current resume. Mount Alexander Shire Council is committed to child safety. We have zero tolerance of child abuse. Our robust human resources, recruitment and vetting practices are strictly adhered to during the application and interviewing process. Applicants should be aware that we conduct working with children, police and reference checks to ensure that we are recruiting the right people. Apply now Email this job Back to top Site Footer Acknowledgement of Country Mount Alexander Shire Council acknowledges that the Traditional Custodians of this land, the Dja Dja Wurrung and Taungurung peoples, proudly survive. We acknowledge their continued practise of custom and their close cultural, spiritual, physical, social, historical and economic relationship with the land and waters that make up their Country, which includes Mount Alexander Shire. Site Footer Contact Us 27 Lyttleton Street Castlemaine, Victoria 3450 Djaara Country View on Map T (03) 5471 1700 E info@mountalexander.vic.gov.au Visit our Contact us page . Site Footer Quick Links Castlemaine, Maldon and Surrounds Mount Alexander Youth Shape Mount Alexander National Relay Service Site Footer Share & Connect Like us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Watch our Youtube Channel Join us on LinkedIn Disclaimer & copyright | Privacy Statement | Sitemap © 2026 Mount Alexander Shire Council | Powered by Granicus IE=edge,chrome=1 #FFFFFF OpenCities - https://granicus.com/product/opencities width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0 yes We are seeking skilled and experienced professional care workers who love supporting people to live independently in the community. This position provides services to Mount Alexander Shire and th