ty information Filming in the shire permit Works on Council land permit Asset protection permit Residential parking permit Accessible parking permit Planning permit Busking permit Open air burn permit Excess animals permit Mobile food business (on Council land) permit Road closure for events permit Community event signage permit Event registration Amend a planning permit Extension of time to a planning permit Siting variation consent application Projections beyond the street alignment consent application Build on flood-prone land consent application Building demolition consent application Building permit Swimming pool or spa registration Certificate of Barrier Compliance Places of public entertainment permit (POPE) Temporary structures permit Fundraising Collecting charitable money or gifts permit Camping on public or private land VicSmart Planning Permit Home / Council / Work with us / Current vacancies / Direct Care Worker (Qualified or Trainee) Direct Care Worker (Qualified or Trainee) Ongoing Applications Reference number 23-DCW Job Type Part Time or Casual Package Band 2 Position Description Position-Description-Direct-Care-Worker-Part-Time-or-Casual.pdf (PDF, 182KB) Part Time or Casual positions Ongoing Band 2 Part time - commencing $63,921 pa (pro-rata) / $33.51 per hour + Super + Allowances Casual - $41.88 per hour (incl. loading) + Super + Allowances Closing Date: Applications are accepted at all times. We are seeking skilled and experienced professional care workers who love supporting people to live independently in the community. We currently provide services in Mount Alexander Shire and Central Goldfields Shire. This is your opportunity to bring your passion and skills to be part of a professional and dedicated team providing high quality in-home support to frail older people and people with disabilities in our community. The role provides tailored services to help clients live healthy, independent and active lives through assistance with daily tasks and activities. Direct Care Worker Traineeship Opportunities: If you don’t already have a certificate III in Individual Support, you can also apply here for a Trainee Direct Care Worker position, to earn and learn on the job. Minimum Qualifications and Experience You must have, or be willing to obtain: Current Police Check Current Working with Children Check Triple vaccinated for COVID (2 doses plus a booster). Current Drivers license and roadworthy, registered and comprehensively insured vehicle for work travel Applicants must be able to work weekends. First Aid and CPR certificate will be gained though training and applied to the role as required If you have any queries or would like to discuss the role, the key contacts are: Sarah Newstead In Home Support Coordinator – East (03) 5471 1845 Talia Jenkin In Home Support Coordinator – West (03) 5471 1728 To apply for a Direct Care Worker or Direct Care Worker Trainee position, please provide a cover letter (no more than 2 pages) outlining why you are interested and the best candidate for this role, and your current resume. Additional information Mount Alexander Shire Council is committed to providing a safe, inclusive, and respectful workplace. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to child safety with zero tolerance for child abuse. We value a diverse workforce and encourage applicants from all cultures, sexual orientations, gender identities and backgrounds. Applicants can expect that the recruitment process will include interviewing, reference checks and criminal history checks. Some positions will also be required to provide a Working with Children Check, and medical assessments including drug and alcohol testing may be undertaken. For more information on the recruitment process, please download the Candidate information document from our website. Apply now Email this job Back to top Site Footer Acknowledgement of Country Mount Alexander Shire Council acknowledges that the Traditional Custodians of this land, the Dja Dja Wurrung and Taungurung peoples, proudly survive. We acknowledge their continued practise of custom and their close cultural, spiritual, physical, social, historical and economic relationship with the land and waters that make up their Country, which includes Mount Alexander Shire. Site Footer Contact Us 27 Lyttleton Street Castlemaine, Victoria 3450 Djaara Country View on Map T (03) 5471 1700 E info@mountalexander.vic.gov.au Visit our Contact us page . Site Footer Quick Links Castlemaine, Maldon and Surrounds Mount Alexander Youth Shape Mount Alexander National Relay Service Site Footer Share & Connect Like us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Watch our Youtube Channel Join us on LinkedIn Disclaimer & copyright | Privacy Statement | Sitemap © 2026 Mount Alexander Shire Council | Powered by Granicus IE=edge,chrome=1 #FFFFFF OpenCities - https://granicus.com/product/opencities width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0 yes We are seeking skilled and experienced professional care workers who love supporting people to live independently in the community. This position provides services to Mount Alexander Shire and the Maryborough region. article https://www.mountalexander.vic.gov.au/Council/Work-with-us/Current-vacancies/Direct-Care-Worker Direct Care Worker (Qualified or Trainee) We are seeking skilled and experienced professional care workers who love supporting people to live independently in the community. This position provides services to Mount Alexander Shire and the Maryborough region. https://www.mountalexander.vic.gov.au/files/ocwebsite/Public/HeroImage/MASC_OGV_2020-social.jpg?w=1200 summary Direct Care Worker (Qualified or Trainee) We are seeking skilled and experienced professional care workers who love supporting people to live independently in the community. This position provides services to Mount Alexander Shire and the Maryborough region. https://www.mountalexander.vic.gov.au/files/ocwebsite/Public/HeroImage/MASC_OGV_2020-social.jpg