may include, grader, grader & combination roller, tractor & combination roller, excavator, backhoe, skid steer and watercart operations. Accurately completing and submitting timesheets, checklists, Safe Work Method Statements (SWMS) and other documentation, in either written or electronic form for both self and those on job site. Maintaining quality standards and obtaining good quality outcomes for the works being performed. Our ideal candidate To be successful in this role you will have: Skills and experience in general road maintenance or civil construction work using heavy equipment. Demonstrated understanding of the basic OH&S principles and practices and environmental considerations on roadsides. Demonstrated ability to work in a team to achieve outcomes. Ability to communicate well with clients, other employees, supervisors and the public. Ability to maintain both written and electronic records as required. Benefits Annual salary increases Nine day fortnight Access to Fitness Passport and Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for staff and families Generous leave provisions, including purchased leave options and paid parental leave Cross-skilling and professional development opportunities Visit the Why work with us page on our website for more benefits. Contact If you have any questions or would like to discuss the role, please contact Grant Farrell, Works Supervisor, on (03) 5471 1700 . How to apply Visit our website and review the Information for applicants , then apply via our Current Vacancies page. Please ensure your application includes: A cover letter, telling us why you are the best person for the position A copy of your current resume Responses to the Key Selection Criteria listed in the position description Additional information Mount Alexander Shire Council is committed to providing a safe, inclusive, and respectful workplace. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to child safety with zero tolerance for child abuse. We value a diverse 