within a road reserve permit Request building plans or property information Filming in the shire permit Works on Council land permit Asset protection permit Residential parking permit Accessible parking permit Planning permit Busking permit Open air burn permit Excess animals permit Mobile food business (on Council land) permit Road closure for events permit Community event signage permit Event registration Amend a planning permit Extension of time to a planning permit Siting variation consent application Projections beyond the street alignment consent application Build on flood-prone land consent application Building demolition consent application Building permit Swimming pool or spa registration Certificate of Barrier Compliance Places of public entertainment permit (POPE) Temporary structures permit Fundraising Collecting charitable money or gifts permit Camping on public or private land VicSmart Planning Permit Home / Council / Work with us / Current vacancies / Social Support Volunteers Social Support Volunteers Ongoing Applications Reference number 23-VOL Job Type Casual Casual Applications are accepted at all times. Mount Alexander Shire is known for its local food and wine, for a vibrant arts community and breathtaking natural surrounds. Perfectly located in Central Victoria, around 30 minutes from Bendigo by car or just 20 by rail, with Melbourne only 90 minutes away, you’ll enjoy a balanced lifestyle with great services, schools and homes in townships like Castlemaine and Maldon. We are seeking volunteers to join our Social Support team. As part of the Community Wellbeing unit, our volunteers assist socially isolated and transport poor older persons to stay socially engaged and active. There are various roles available including home visitors, mini-bus drivers, cards and scrabble players, and people to help make tea and coffee. How much time you want to commit is up to you, from as little as one hour, to ten or more hours per week. The roles involve working with vulnerable people and police checks and some basic training will be required. Any training, including first aid, will be provided and paid for by Council. Mount Alexander Shire Council is a Centrelink Approved Voluntary Work Organisation. If you have any queries or would like to discuss the role, please contact Julia Leonard, Business Support Officer - Home Support (03) 5471 1797 or email j.leonard@mountalexander.vic.gov.au . Mount Alexander Shire Council is committed to child safety. We have zero tolerance of child abuse. Our robust human resources, recruitment and vetting practices are strictly adhered to during the application and interviewing process. Applicants should be aware that we conduct working with children, police and reference checks to ensure that we are recruiting the right people. Apply now Email this job Back to top Acknowledgement of Country Mount Alexander Shire Council acknowledges that the Traditional Custodians of this land, the Dja Dja Wurrung and Taungurung peoples, proudly survive. We acknowledge their continued practise of custom and their close cultural, spiritual, physical, social, historical and economic relationship with the land and waters that make up their Country, which includes Mount Alexander Shire. Contact Us 27 Lyttleton Street Castlemaine, Victoria 3450 Djaara Country View on Map T (03) 5471 1700 E info@mountalexander.vic.gov.au Visit our Contact us page . Quick Links Castlemaine, Maldon and Surrounds Mount Alexander Youth Shape Mount Alexander National Relay Service Share & Connect Like us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Watch our Youtube Channel Join us on LinkedIn Disclaimer & copyright | Privacy Statement | Sitemap © 2026 Mount Alexander Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
