n. Deliver impactful economic development initiatives, support local business growth and attract new investment, coordinate business training and events, build partnerships with industry, government, and the community. To be successful in this role you will need Qualifications Essential Employee working with children check Current Victorian driver licence Desirable Tertiary degree level qualification in a business, management or marketing related discipline is preferred Experience Desirable Several years’ professional experience preferred, ideally within a small business environment. Experience in local government Key selection criteria 1 Relationship building and business engagement Demonstrated ability to build and maintain effective relationships with local businesses, industry groups and community stakeholders, and provide responsive support that contributes to business growth and economic development outcomes. Key selection criteria 2 Research, analysis and reporting Demonstrated research and analytical skills, including the ability to interpret economic data and prepare reports to inform strategic planning, decision-making and funding opportunities. Key selection criteria 3 Planning and organisational skills Demonstrated ability to plan, prioritise and manage multiple tasks, work both independently and collaboratively, and deliver outcomes within agreed timeframes. Applications that fail to address the above key selection criteria will not be considered for this position. For more information A full position description, the key selection criteria and information on how to apply can be found in the information package, or by requesting a copy from customer service on 1300 656 564. For further information about the position or duties involved, please contact Jo Mackenzie, coordinator economic development and tourism on 0407 591 052 or jo.mackenzie@moyne.vic.gov.au Postal applications Confidential – Economic Development Officer People and Culture Coordinator Moy