 Business Opportunities Advocacy and Partnerships Governance and Transparency Corporate Documents Financial Sustainability Roadmap Why work for Murrindindi Shire Council Hear from our employees Reasons to work with us Values Our values underpin everything we do. Our focus is to be a high performing organisation providing great service to our communities through: Accountability Showing leadership at all levels accepting responsibility for our decisions and actions. Managing Council's resources responsibly and operating within our means. Work will be directed by clear objectives and we will deliver what we promise. Empathy Caring for our colleagues and our community. Treating others fairly, objectively and without bias or discrimination. Not tolerating the harassment or bullying of others. Making decisions that are consistent with the promotion and support of human rights. Integrity Demonstrating honesty and integrity through open and transparent actions. Through our actions we will strive to maintain the highest levels of trust from our community. Reporting improper conduct and will avoid any General or Material conflict of interest. Exercising our authority with consistency and responsibility. Professionalism Providing frank, impartial and timely advice to Council and others. Striving to provide an exemplary level of service at all times. Striving to continuously improve service delivery and outcomes for our community. Variety Murrindindi Shire is situated on Melbourne's peri-urban fringe and encompasses the charming rural townships of Alexandra, Eildon, Kinglake, Marysville and Yea. The Shire benefits from great natural beauty and tourist attractions such as Lake Eildon, picturesque national parks, the Great Victorian Rail Trail and access to Victoria's snowfields. We are located within proximity to Melbourne, a lovely 60 to 90 minute drive from Melbourne, depending on your route. We have Council Offices in Alexandra, Yea and Kinglake to improve accessibility to our community. Opportunities We offer a supportive flexible work environment within a supportive team along with ongoing professional development and a range of employee benefits designed to promote a positive work/life balance. A career with us means a wealth of opportunities. Every project you work on will enhance your skills and capabilities. The diverse communities within Murrindindi Shire means that you will tackle a range of complex and outcome-focused projects. Culture Murrindindi Shire Council provides a diverse range of services to the community. Our roles vary to include both indoor and outdoor roles from administrative, engineering, planning, parks and gardens, maintenance, resource recovery centres, community engagement and management opportunities. This is achieved through flexible working options including compressed hours, job sharing, part-time working and other flexible work settings up to 50% of the week. Council offers benefits to employees that aim to create a supportive and rewarding work environment, helping employees to thrive both professionally and personally . There is a key focus on health and wellbeing with access to confidential counselling and initiatives to support physical and mental health. We have policies supporting adoption and parental leave and support opportunities for continuous learning and career development, including training programs, mentoring, and relevant tuition reimbursement. We care strongly about creating a collaborative workplace where our employees feel valued, respected, and empowered and we are committed to providing equal opportunity regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, different backgrounds or life stage. Everyone is an important part of our team. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion At Murrindindi Shire Council, we are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace where everyone is welcome. We actively promote gender equity and equality in our workplace and practices and encourage people of all genders, cultures, backgrounds, and abilities to apply for positions with us. Our commitment is to find a balance of modern flexible work arrangements that can support your needs including full-time, part-time, hybrid, and job-sharing options. Additionally, we are dedicated to fostering a culturally safe workplace and to protecting children from abuse in accordance with the Victorian Child Safe Standards and Council’s Child Safety and Wellbeing Policy. . Murrindindi Shire Council Enterprise Agreement All employees are covered by the Murrindindi Shire Council Enterprise Agreement No 9 2022. The Enterprise Agreement outlines employee entitlements, remuneration and conditions of employment. Read and download a full copy of the Murrindindi Shire Council Enterprise Agreement No 9 2022 (PDF, 3MB) . Within the Enterprise Agreement, there are two reference awards: Victorian Local Government Award 2015 Nurses (ANMF - Victorian Local Government) Award 2015 Was this page helpful? * (required) Help us improve this site Yes Maybe No How can we improve this page? Email address * (required) Type the characters you see in the image below * (Required) Generate new image Read aloud Please enter the text in the image Back to top Acknowledgement of Country Murrindindi Shire Council is proud to acknowledge the Taungurung and Wurundjeri Woi-wurrung people as the Traditional Owners of the land we now call Murrindindi Shire. We pay our respects to First Nations leaders and Elders, past, present and emerging, who are the keepers of history, traditions, knowledge and culture of this land. We commit to working in collaboration with Traditional Owners of this land in a spirit of reconciliation and partnership. Contact Us Murrindindi Shire Council PO Box 138 Alexandra VIC 3714 Australia Phone: (03) 5772 0333 Email: customer@murrindindi.vic.gov.au View full contact information ABN: 83 600 647 004 Share & Connect Like us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Foll