 (PDF, 1MB) Full Time, Permanent Band 3 plus 12% Superannuation Work in a supportive team environment responding to priority requests Make a significant difference in our community Murrindindi Shire Council has an exciting opportunity for a Rapid Response Officer to join our Parks and Gardens team in an important role which responds to our urgent maintenance activities. This role focuses on priority service issues to ensure they are addressed in a timely and responsive manner. About this opportunity In this role you will take timely and appropriate action to make safe hazards relating to Council roads and park assets including actions such as the removal of branches and other obstructions to roads and path, control and clean up of spills, replacing missing service pit lids, road and park signage, removal of dead animals and urgent road pothole remediation. When not undertaking urgent response works you will be involved in general roads, parks and garden maintenance activities, including removal of graffiti, bins, herbicide spraying, signage and maintenance, tree pruning and general gardening duties. What you will bring We are seeking someone who has demonstrated experience or can bring: a trade, works or service environment organisation of own work to meet timelines and set standards a current Victorian Drivers Licence and Medium Rigid Truck Licence various plant operator competencies (desirable) e.g. skid steer loader, tractor good interpersonal skills and a team player with ability to follow direction a capacity to engage and deal effectively with the general public as required; and the ability to work weekends and public holiday, based on a monthly roster as required. What we offer Murrindindi Shire is situated on Melbourne's peri-urban fringe and encompasses the charming rural townships of Alexandra, Eildon, Kinglake, Marysville and Yea. The Shire benefits from great natural beauty and tourist attractions such as Lake Eildon, picturesque national parks, the Great Victorian Rail Trail and access to Victoria's snowfields. We are located within proximity to Melbourne, a lovely 60 to 90 minute drive from Melbourne, depending on your route. We offer a supportive and flexible work environment within a supportive team along with ongoing professional development and a range of employee benefits designed to promote a positive work/life balance. How to apply For more information about the role or a confidential discussion, please contact Asset Maintenance Coordinator Melissa Spinks on (03 5772 0333.) We request your application contains a cover letter, your resume, and addresses the key selection criteria set out in the Position Description You can submit your application and any accompanying attachments: online – you will receive an email notification confirming your submission by email to msc@murrindindi.vic.gov.au or post them to Murrindindi Shire Council, PO Box 138, Alexandra 3714. Applications close at 11.45 pm, on Sunday 7 June 2026 Conditions of employment are in accordance with Murrindindi Shire Council’s Enterprise Agreement. It is also a condition of employment that the successful applicant: provides evidence of eligibility to work in Australia undertakes a satisfactory Police Check. Fitness for work / Pre-Employment Medical Check. provides evidence of a valid drivers licence. Online Job Application Form Email this job Back to top Acknowledgement of Country Murrindindi Shire Council is proud to acknowledge the Taungurung and Wurundjeri Woi-wurrung people as the Traditional Owners of the land we now call Murrindindi Shire. We pay our respects to First Nations leaders and Elders, past, present and emerging, who are the keepers of history, traditions, knowledge and culture of this land. We commit to working in collaboration with Traditional Owners of this land in a spirit of reconciliation and partnership. Contact Us Murrindindi Shire Council PO Box 138 Alexandra VIC 3714 Australia Phone: (03) 5772 0333 Email: customer@murri