    {
      "advertised_salary_max": 24.0,
      "advertised_salary_min": 15.0,
      "advertised_salary_text": "Nillumbik Shire Council - Recruitment Hub - Other opportunities Toggle navigation Home About us Awards Current vacancies Staff benefits Contact us Other opportunities Other opportunities Local jobs for local people Council is partnered with Melbourne's North Joblink which provides a free service to both businesses and residents in Melbourne's North. It seeks to connect businesses in Melbourne's North with the region's talent to make living, working and employing in Melbourne's North a reality. Jobseekers can register for the portal to be advised when local positions are advertised. To find out more, go to Melbourne's North Joblink website YConnect This program is supported by JobsVic and is available to young people aged 15-24 in Nillumbik. It gives them the support and training they need to start out on their career path and find sustainable employment. There is a team of 20 mentors spread across Melbourne who can support young people. The mentors themselves represent quite a diverse group in terms of age, gender and ethnicity, which is a tremendous asset and enables them to be able to connect with and relate to young people. YConnect also develop connections and relations with employers to identify their recruitment and staffing needs so they can steer program participants towards areas of alignment as potential candidates. To find out more, go to YConnect Work experience Council’s work experience program provides students with an understanding of local government and exposure to a formal work environment. To find out more, go to our Work Experience Page Volunteering Discover a range of volunteering opportunities in and around Nillumbik that you could get involved with. To find out more, go to our Volunteering Page Casual Employment On occasions we have casual employment opportunities which could be from one day up to 3 months. We use a managed services provider (Comensura). For future casual employment opportunities, please register with any of our recruitment partners and let them know you are interested in working at Nillumbik. Our Recruitment Partners: Aspect ATEL Hays Horner Inspired McArthur Planned Business Public Sector People Randstad Work Solutions About us We achieve extraordinary outcomes for our community - Find out more here! Learn about Nillumbik Vacancies We are always looking for new talent to join our team - See what's on offer! See the jobs on offer! Staff Benefits See what makes working at the Nillumbik Shire Council great. Working in our team! Powered by Talent PropellerTM Home About us Awards Current vacancies Staff benefits Contact us Other opportunities Privacy Policy",
