s and valuations How rates are calculated How to pay your rates Understanding your rates notice Rebates and exemptions Emergency Services and Volunteers Fund Financial hardship assistance Changing your details Property valuations General Frequently Asked Questions Planning Services Statutory Planning Strategic Planning Roads and Streets Asset management Capital Works Program Roads and streets Legal point of discharge Works within road reserves Photography & Videography Public health services Aquatic Facilities information Environmental nuisances Food premises and food events Food safety complaints Septic systems and wastewater services Hair, Beauty, Tattooing and Skin Penetration Business Pests Public health fees and charges Prescribed Accommodation VicRoads services Events All Events Calendar Tourism and Events Grants Major Tourism Events Partnership Program Tourism Events Grant Community Events Grant Planning Your Event Register Your Event Promote Your Event Venues, Parks & Recreation Areas for Hire Tourism Events 2026 Northern Grampians Easter Festival Emergency Council's role Get prepared Types of emergencies Fire Flood Storm Extreme heat Power outage Infectious disease Recovery initiatives 2024 Grampians Bushfires October 2022 Floods Glenorchy Flood Recovery Municipal Emergency Management Planning Committee Municipal Fire Management Plan Search Home / Working at Northern Grampians Shire Council Working at Northern Grampians Shire Council If you want to make a difference and be part of a challenging, flexible and rewarding team, joining Northern Grampians might be the right career move for you. You will have great opportunities to discover and share innovative thinking, take on exciting challenges and carve your own career pathway. About Our Team Great reasons to work for us Our employees work at Northern Grampians Shire Council because they are passionate, collaborative and committed to both the community and the work they do. The scale and diversity of the work that local government is required to deliver means that there are many different career opportunities and pathways available within the organisation. These include: Engineering Roads, bridges and drainage Planning Early childhood services Environment and sustainability Community development and wellbeing and many others. Because we are a smaller organisation, we can provide you with opportunities to act in leadership roles, transition between teams and participate in a range of collaborative projects with other team members or the wider community. We provide a supportive and flexible environment that values the balance between work and our employees' personal lives. We work with our staff to develop working arrangements that enable them to accommodate their personal commitments and enjoy all that our communities have to offer. Our progressive activity-based work environment allows our employees to choose where they work each day. We provide a variety of different work spaces , including quiet areas for tasks that require a high level of concentration, and collaboration rooms to facilitate the sharing of ideas. We also provide sit-stand desks to ensure our employees are comfortable while they work. In addition to supporting the development of the community you live in, there are many other benefits to working in local government. These include: Ongoing training and personal development opportunities Hybrid work arrangements (including remote working) for eligible roles and flexible start and finish times Rostered or accrued days off for full-time staff 16 weeks paid parental leave for primary carers regardless of gender Ability to purchase up to four weeks additional leave each year Gradual increase or decrease in hours to support transition from parental leave or to retirement Access to paid leave for assisted reproductive treatment, gender transition or to respond to family violence Salary sacrificing including novated leases Discounted gym membership An employee assistance counselling program To successfully deliver our services, we need talented, committed employees across a range of skilled, trade, professional and managerial roles. We offer career development opportunities through graduate placements, apprenticeships, traineeships, work experience and career progression. Equality, access and Inclusion Diversity, Equity and Inclusion At Northern Grampians Shire Council, we are proud to be an inclusive and diverse employer of choice. We believe that a diverse workforce brings a wealth of knowledge, skills, and perspectives that enrich our organisation and the communities we serve. We encourage people from all walks of life to apply for positions with us. We understand that imposter syndrome can affect individuals from all backgrounds, and we want to assure those who may experience it that their unique talents and contributions are valued and welcomed at our council and we encourage you to apply. We provide a supportive and nurturing environment where everyone can thrive and grow. As a child safe organisation, we are committed to creating a safe and inclusive environment for all. We actively promote accessible and flexible working arrangements to ensure that everyone, including people with disabilities, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, culturally, religiously, and linguistically diverse people, young people, older people, women, and people who identify as LGBTQIA+, can participate fully in our workforce. We take pride in our diversity and recognise that it is a source of strength. We embrace new approaches and celebrate the contributions made by everyone. Join us at Northern Grampians Shire Council and be part of a team that values and respects the unique perspectives and experiences of all individuals. Together, we can make a positive impact on our community. . Core Values Core Values Our Values are at the core of Northern Grampians Shire Council's culture. They define who we are and what we stand for. They provide the framework for how we treat each other and our customers. We live by them and make sure they are built into our everyday practice. Northern Grampians Shire Council is: Responsive : we will engage with all stakeholders and listen and respond appropriately to your needs. Innovative : we will be positive and endeavour to find solutions and choice in our service delivery. Continuous Improvement: we will continually strive, within our means, for best possible practice and improvement in service delivery. Prompt : we will respond promptly, within agreed timeframes, to all of your requests. Respectful : we will be respectful and conscious of diversity and make available information and services in an accessible and inclusive manner. Contact us Have any further questions about working at NGSC? Ph: 03 5358 8700 Email: ngshire@ngshire.vic.gov.au Current job listings See our current vacancies here >> Our region Find out more information about the Northern Grampians region here >> Photo gallery Check out the beautiful surrounds you will have when working with us. Photo gallery >> Was this page helpful? * (required) Help us improve this site Yes Maybe No How can we improve this page? Given name/s Last name Email address Would you like to be contacted about this? Yes No Type the characters you see in the image below * (Required) Generate new image Read aloud Please enter the text in the image Share Facebook X Print Email Back to top Contact us Stawell Customer Support Stawell Town Hall 59-69 Main St, Stawell, Victoria, Australia, 3380 View map St Arnaud Customer Support St Arnaud Town Hall 40 Napier St, St Arnaud, Victoria, Australia, 3478 View map Phone us: 03 5358 8700 Email us: ngshire@ngshire.vic.gov.au Postal Address : PO Box 580, Stawell, VIC, 3380 Prevention of Family Violence Northern Grampians Shire Council has a responsibility to work toward prevention of family violence before it happens and promote prevention in the community. If you would like further information, click here . If you need support please call 1800 RESPECT or if you or someone you know is in immediate danger or requires assistance from Victoria Police please call 000. Share and connect Like us on Facebook Watch our YouTube Channel Instagram Disclaimer and copyright | Privacy statement | Sitemap | A-Z index | Terms and Conditions © 2026 Northern Grampians Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
