Forms, Resources and FAQs Strategic planning and major projects Flood Studies Township Plans Planning Scheme Review Renewables projects in Pyrenees Bushfire Recovery Planning Program How the Bushfire Recovery Planning Program works Bushfire Recovery Planning Program FAQs Consultants and Surveyors Small second homes Home / About Us / Work for Council / Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities Council has a diverse workforce of over 100 full time, part time and casual staff. If you are interested in joining our team, we are interested in hearing from you. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Council welcomes applications from all members of our community and those outside the area too. The Pyrenees Shire Council is an inclusive and an equal opportunity employer. Council offers a range of flexible work arrangements and people of all abilities and backgrounds are encouraged to apply. If you are excited about a particular role, but your experience doesn’t perfectly align to the criteria we encourage you to apply for the position regardless or to have a confidential conversation with the contact person for the position. A Recruitment Information Pack has been created to provide you with information relating to the application and selection process. Click here to view (PDF, 535KB) Why work for Council? Council provides competitive remuneration packages including attractive salaries, hours, employee benefits and training and development opportunities. Click here to find out more Current Vacancies 1 Result(s) Found Parks and Gardens Maintenance Operator Applications closing on Tuesday, 09 June 2026 Full Time (Permanent) Council is seeking a motivated and reliable Parks and Gardens Maintenance Operator to join the Works team based in Beaufort. Page 1 Page 1 of 1 Search Jobs By Phrase or Keyword By Job Type Any Job Type Full Time (Permanent) Full Time (Short Term) Part Time (Permanent) Part Time (Short Term) Part Time (Temporary) Casual Contract Volunteer Was this page helpful? * (required) Help us improve this site Yes Maybe No How can we improve this page? Email address Type the characters you see in the image below * (Required) Generate new image Read aloud Please enter the text in the image Back to top Council office location Our Council is located at: 5 Lawrence Street BEAUFORT VIC 3373 Phone: 1300 PYRENEES (1300 797 363) Fax: (03) 5349 2068 Email: pyrenees@pyrenees.vic.gov.au Indigenous Acknowledgement We acknowledge the people past and present of the Wadawurrung, Dja Dja Wurrung, Eastern Maar, Wotjobaluk, Jaadwa, Jadawadjali, Wergaia and Jupagulk Nations, whose land and waters the Pyrenees Shire operates on. We pay our respects to their Ancestors and Elders, recognise and respect their customs, stewardship and continuing connection to Country. Follow us on Social Media Like us on facebook Watch our YouTube Channel Instagram LinkedIn Disclaimer & Copyright | Privacy Statement | Sitemap | A - Z Index | Search © 2026 Pyrenees Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
