n Application Forms, Resources and FAQs Strategic planning and major projects Flood Studies Township Plans Planning Scheme Review Renewables projects in Pyrenees Bushfire Recovery Planning Program How the Bushfire Recovery Planning Program works Bushfire Recovery Planning Program FAQs Consultants and Surveyors Small second homes Home / About Us / Work for Council / Employment Opportunities / Parks and Gardens Maintenance Operator Parks and Gardens Maintenance Operator Applications closing on 09 June 2026, 12:00 PM Reference Number 48/22/494 Job Type Full Time (Permanent) Package Band 3 (Salary $66,877 - $71,485 incl. RDO) + Super & Allowance Position Description Position-Description-Parks-and-Gardens-Maintenance-Operator-May-2026.pdf (PDF, 479KB) Parks and Gardens Maintenance Operator Permanent Full time Band 3 or Band 4 (depending on relevant horticulture qualifications) (Salary $66,877 - $71,485 incl. RDO) + Super & Allowance The Pyrenees Shire Council is seeking a motivated and reliable Parks and Gardens Maintenance Operator to join the Works team based in Beaufort. This full-time role is primarily responsible for the maintenance of Councils parks and gardens, and will include garden maintenance, mowing tree maintenance and spraying of weeds and pests. Other maintenance activities may include, but not limited to, litter control, street sweeping, drainage maintenance and street furniture maintenance. The ideal candidate will be a team player with a sound understanding of workplace safety requirements who has practical experience in horticultural activities and experience operating and maintaining parks and gardens mowers and associated equipment. Please refer to the Position Description for the comprehensive details about the role. Should you then require any further information not covered in the advertisement or in the position description, contact Glenn Deaker, Manager Works on 1300 797 363. How to Apply: Interested candidates can download the position description and complete the Employment Application Questionnaire via the link on this page. Application Deadline : Applications for this position close at 12pm Tuesday 9 June 2026. For any enquiries regarding the application process, please contact Chantelle Sandlant at pyrenees@pyrenees.vic.gov.au or by phone at 1300 797 363. Pyrenees Shire Council is proud to be an inclusive and equal opportunity employer. We offer flexible work arrangements and welcome applications from individuals of all abilities and backgrounds. J Nolan Chief Executive Officer Employment Application Questionnaire - Parks & Gardens Email this job Was this page helpful? * (required) Help us improve this site Yes Maybe No How can we improve this page? Email address Type the characters you see in the image below * (Required) Generate new image Read aloud Please enter the text in the image Back to top Council office location Our Council is located at: 5 Lawrence Street BEAUFORT VIC 3373 Phone: 1300 PYRENEES (1300 797 363) Fax: (03) 5349 2068 Email: pyrenees@pyrenees.vic.gov.au Indigenous Acknowledgement We acknowledge the people past and present of the Wadawurrung, Dja Dja Wurrung, Eastern Maar, Wotjobaluk, Jaadwa, Jadawadjali, Wergaia and Jupagulk Nations, whose land and waters the Pyrenees Shire operates on. We pay our respects to their Ancestors and Elders, recognise and respect their customs, stewardship and continuing connection to Country. Follow us on Social Media Like us on facebook Watch our YouTube Channel Instagram LinkedIn Disclaimer & Copyright | Privacy Statement | Sitemap | A - Z Index | Search © 2026 Pyrenees Shire Council | Powered by Granicus",
