      "advertised_salary_period": "week",
      "advertised_salary_text": "Careers at Council | Strathbogie Shire Longwood bushfire community information and updates - CLICK HERE! Longwood bushfire community information and updates - CLICK HERE! ++ Increase text size -- Decrease text size Favourites Contact Skip to main content Home Council About Our Council Careers at Council Council Meetings and Minutes Mayor and Councillors Executive Leadership New Residents Maps Taungurung Land and Waters Council Plans, Policies, Strategies and Reports Advocacy Share Strathbogie: Have your say News and Newsletters Latest News Community Update eNews Contact Us Report an Issue and Make a Request Governance Audit and Risk Committee Public Registers Freedom Of Information Privacy and Accessibility Major Projects Tenders Payments and Infringements Make a Payment Infringement Internal Review Community Volunteer Volunteer with Council Volunteer with Community Action Groups Local Legends Accessibility Accessible Public Toilets Accessible Parking Permits Health and Wellbeing Grants and Funding Community Grants Event Grants Youth Council Youth Spaces Youth Crews L2P Learner Driver Program Strathbogie Amplify Families and Children Immunisations Maternal Child Health Playgroups and Kindergartens Pets and Livestock Pets for adoption Adoption Process Missing/Lost Pets Domestic Animal Business Register My Pet Keeping Animals Livestock Family Violence Domestic Animal Support Arts and Culture ARTBOX Services Building and Planning Building Pools and Spas Wastewater Disposal Systems Planning Planning Permits Development Plans Planning Applications Currently Advertised Sustainable Subdivisions Framework (SSF) Planning Scheme Amendment Proposed Updated Flood Controls Rates How To Read Your Rates and Valuation Notice Rates FAQs Public Health Local Laws Business Support Business Permits and Development Directory Good Access = Good Business Promote My Business or Group Roads and Grading Rubbish Kerbside Collection Transfer Stations Kerbside Service Requests Nagambie Tip Shop How do I dispose of? Emergency Management Local Emergency Action Plans (LEAPs) Floods 2022 Prepare and Plan Act and Respond Relief and Recovery Drought 2025 Things to do Sport and Recreation Nagambie Splash Park Facilities Sporting Grounds Swimming Pools Parks and Playgrounds Skateparks Tracks and Trails Libraries Euroa Community Cinema Boating and Fishing Boating Fishing in Nagambie and the Strathbogie Shire Our Waterways Tourism Accommodation Food and Wine Geocaching Markets Our History Our Attractions Visitor Information Centres Events Filming and Photography Nagambie Lakes Regatta Centre Hold an Event Whats On Environment Goulburn Murray Solar Savers Vegetation Removal Climate Action Greening Euroa Gardening Careers at Council Home / About Our Council / Careers at Council Strathbogie Shire Council is one of the largest employers in the area, offering a diverse range of roles both within our outdoor operational team and indoor staff. If you are interested in taking on a career with Strathbogie Shire Council, view the list of vacancies below and follow the instructions to apply. Our Council is a vibrant and progressive rural municipality located within two hours from the Melbourne CBD along the Hume Freeway. The Shire is in immediate proximity to major regional towns Seymour, Shepparton, Wangaratta and Benalla which offer all of the facilities, retail and entertainment opportunities you would find in a capital city – but with the peaceful country atmosphere. Employee Benefits Why you will love working at Strathbogie Shire Council.... We understand the need for flexibility and can offer: Hybrid working arrangements – up to 40% working from home Option for working more hours over less days (e.g., 9-day fortnight) Negotiated start and finish times We have generous leave entitlements including: 3 additional days of Family Care Leave per year to support caring requirements 3 days paid leave during Christmas closure Long service leave available pro rata after five years, and transferable across local government organisations Up to 10 days unpaid leave per year for Cultural and Ceremonial Leave Up to 20 days of paid Family Violence Leave annually Parental Leave – 16 weeks of paid leave for primary carer and 2 weeks for secondary carer, with option to be taken a half pay We value your health and wellbeing and offer: Access to the Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Income Protection Scheme for all employees Weekly onsite visits for treatment of soft tissue injuries Annual Flu Vaccinations Access to Local Government Employees Health Plan We encourage professional development and learning opportunities including: Support to study with a repayment plan via payroll deductions Access to study leave On the job training And the bonuses: Annual pay increases in line with our Enterprise Agreement 17.5% Leave Loading paid annually as a lump sum ‘Christmas bonus’ Recognition awards for years of service Volunteer Programs → Click here to fill out a Volunteer Application Form Strathbogie Shire Council has many dedicated volunteers who contribute hours of valuable work for our organisation every year. Through volunteering with Council, you can bring your skills and passions to meaningful roles that have a clear and positive benefit to the community. Volunteering is also a great way to learn new skills, develop new friendships, and feel a part of your community. Euroa Community Cinema The Euroa Community Cinema volunteers perform a wide range of roles to deliver a vibrant, diverse and entertaining cinema program to the community – plus, cinema volunteers get in free to watch the movie screening when on duty. Nagambie Lakes Visitor Information Centre & Euroa Hub Tourist and Resident Information The Visitor Information Centres (VICs) provide a valuable service for both residents and visitors to the Shire. Volunteers are the first point of contact for visitors and assist them by answering a range of queries such as the location of butchers, mechanics, caravan repairers, restaurants and supermarkets. They give guidance on the region’s attractions, things to see and do, directions around the district, accommodation, conference venues, retailers as well as information about Victoria. The centres also have a calendar of events which is useful when planning an event, or even a wedding. Volunteering at the centres is perfect for those who have a passion for their region Various Working Groups Keep an eye on our online engagement platform www.share.strathbogie.vic.gov.au for opportunities throughout the year to join various working groups. There is always an opportunity to stay engaged in Council’s projects through this platform. Current vacancies Team Member – Operations Closing date: July 13, 2026 Full time, on-going, Euroa based Fortnightly RDO Band 3 + industry allowance - $65,413 per annum+ 12% superannuation About Us:... Jobs Category Operations Location Euroa Victoria, 3666 Position Description About Our Council Careers at Council Council Meetings and Minutes Archived Council Meeting Minutes and Agendas – Pre Jan 2021 Executive Leadership Maps Mayor and Councillors New Residents Taungurung Land and Waters Council Back to top Add to Favourites rate this page Did you find this page useful? Good Bad Sign up to receive our eNews Subscribe We acknowledge the Traditional Custodians of the places we live, work and play. We recognise and respect the enduring relationship they have with their lands and waters, and we pay respects to the Elders past, present and emerging Home Council Services Local Laws Things to do Environment Follow us Facebook Instagram YouTube QUICK LINKS Contact Council Submit a Request Find a Business, Club or Group Make a Payment Current Tenders Building and Planning Interactive Maps Transfer Stations and Bin Days Current Jobs © 2026 Strathbogie Shire Council Privacy Policy Terms & Conditions",
