      "advertised_salary_period": "week",
      "advertised_salary_text": "Team Member Operations Longwood bushfire community information and updates - CLICK HERE! Longwood bushfire community information and updates - CLICK HERE! ++ Increase text size -- Decrease text size Favourites Contact Skip to main content Home Council About Our Council Careers at Council Council Meetings and Minutes Mayor and Councillors Executive Leadership New Residents Maps Taungurung Land and Waters Council Plans, Policies, Strategies and Reports Advocacy Share Strathbogie: Have your say News and Newsletters Latest News Community Update eNews Contact Us Report an Issue and Make a Request Governance Audit and Risk Committee Public Registers Freedom Of Information Privacy and Accessibility Major Projects Tenders Payments and Infringements Make a Payment Infringement Internal Review Community Volunteer Volunteer with Council Volunteer with Community Action Groups Local Legends Accessibility Accessible Public Toilets Accessible Parking Permits Health and Wellbeing Grants and Funding Community Grants Event Grants Youth Council Youth Spaces Youth Crews L2P Learner Driver Program Strathbogie Amplify Families and Children Immunisations Maternal Child Health Playgroups and Kindergartens Pets and Livestock Pets for adoption Adoption Process Missing/Lost Pets Domestic Animal Business Register My Pet Keeping Animals Livestock Family Violence Domestic Animal Support Arts and Culture ARTBOX Services Building and Planning Building Pools and Spas Wastewater Disposal Systems Planning Planning Permits Development Plans Planning Applications Currently Advertised Sustainable Subdivisions Framework (SSF) Planning Scheme Amendment Proposed Updated Flood Controls Rates How To Read Your Rates and Valuation Notice Rates FAQs Public Health Local Laws Business Support Business Permits and Development Directory Good Access = Good Business Promote My Business or Group Roads and Grading Rubbish Kerbside Collection Transfer Stations Kerbside Service Requests Nagambie Tip Shop How do I dispose of? Emergency Management Local Emergency Action Plans (LEAPs) Floods 2022 Prepare and Plan Act and Respond Relief and Recovery Drought 2025 Things to do Sport and Recreation Nagambie Splash Park Facilities Sporting Grounds Swimming Pools Parks and Playgrounds Skateparks Tracks and Trails Libraries Euroa Community Cinema Boating and Fishing Boating Fishing in Nagambie and the Strathbogie Shire Our Waterways Tourism Accommodation Food and Wine Geocaching Markets Our History Our Attractions Visitor Information Centres Events Filming and Photography Nagambie Lakes Regatta Centre Hold an Event Whats On Environment Goulburn Murray Solar Savers Vegetation Removal Climate Action Greening Euroa Gardening Team Member – Operations Home / Council / Careers at Council / Team Member – Operations Team Member – Operations Full time, on-going, Euroa based Fortnightly RDO Band 3 + industry allowance – $65,413 per annum+ 12% superannuation About Us: The Strathbogie Shire is a vibrant and progressive rural municipality located about two hours from the Melbourne CBD along the Hume Highway. We have diverse and picturesque communities served by townships such as Euroa, Nagambie, Violet Town, Avenel, Longwood, Ruffy and Strathbogie. About the Role: We are seeking a highly motivated individual, who takes pride and care in their work to join our Operations team in this integral role. Tasks that you will be undertaking include but are not limited to, construction, re-construction, maintenance and repairs of roads, bridges, culverts, drainage, footpaths, parks, reserves, gardens and playgrounds. Our ideal candidate will have: To be successful you will have previous relevant experience or transferable skills that align with municipal and/or civil work environments, hold a Medium Rigid licence, be available for after-hours emergency work, and be committed to the safety of themselves and others. Additional licences and experience operating various plant would also be highly regarded. Why you will love working at Strathbogie Shire Council: We have generous leave entitlements including: 3 additional days Family Care Leave per year to support caring requirements. 3 days paid leave during Christmas closure. Long service leave available pro rata after five years and transferable across local government organisations. Up to 10 days unpaid leave per year for Cultural and Ceremonial Leave. Up to 20 days of paid Family Violence Leave annually. Parental leave – 16 weeks of paid leave for primary carer and 2 weeks for secondary carer, with the option to be taken at half pay. We value your health and wellbeing and offer: Access to the Employee Assistance Program (EAP). Income Protection Scheme for all employees. Weekly onsite visits for treatment of soft tissue injuries. Annual Flu Vaccinations. Access to Local Government Employee Health Plan. We encourage professional development and learning opportunities including: Support to study with a repayment plan via payroll deductions. Access to study leave. On the job training. And the bonuses: Annual pay increases in line with our Enterprise Agreement. 17.5% Leave Loading paid out annually as a lump sum “Christmas bonus”. Recognition awards for years of service. For further information about this position, please contact Gavin Williams – Operations Coordinator on 5795 0000. Click here to view the position description . Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis Strathbogie Shire Council is an equal opportunity employer and a Child Safe organisation. We value diversity in our workplace and will consider flexible working arrangements. Job Application Form \" * \" indicates required fields Comments This field is for validation purposes and should be left unchanged. First Name * Last Name * Preferred Name (if applicable) Gender * Select Gender Male Female Non-binary Email * Contact Number * Street Address * City/Town * Postcode * State * Select state New South Wales Queensland Northern