      "advertised_salary_max": 202.0,
      "advertised_salary_min": 25.0,
      "advertised_salary_period": "year",
      "advertised_salary_text": "Careers | Yarra City Council Skip to main content Search Menu Close Home About us Careers Careers Join our team and help us better serve our diverse community. We're committed to ensuring our Yarra continues to thrive as a vibrant, creative, safe and inclusive environment for all of us to live and work. We have a bold ambition outlined in our Council Plan to make Yarra more climate-safe, equitable and liveable in the future. To achieve our ambition, we need the best people who share our values. See our open roles Learn about volunteering with Yarra Our values Accountability We own what we do and expect others to as well. Respect We include all and diversity is our strength. Courage We are intentional in our actions and seek the brave path. If you care about making a real difference and being part of a team that is passionate about building community spirit, supporting diversity, making connections to each other and creating a more sustainable future - then, we want to hear from you! Why you should join our team We offer a range of benefits, and have also made significant commitments to diversity, inclusion and gender equity. Expand All Collapse All Competitive salaries and perks 17.5% annual leave loading paid prior to Christmas each year free professional counselling through a world-class Employee Assistance Program (EAP) access to health and wellbeing programs, including discounted rates for Yarra aquatic and leisure centres and salary sacrifice offered for Yarra childcare access to free LinkedIn learning courses discounted yearly Myki card Flexible working hybrid working model rostered day off (RDO) for many positions 16 days personal leave per year 18 weeks parental leave and 3 weeks for non-primary caregivers 40 hours pre-natal leave per pregnancy 5 days compassionate leave per occasion 3 days culture leave per year plus 5 days unpaid leave community service and armed forces leave up to an additional 10 weeks of purchased leave or career break 20 days of family violence leave and 5 days for employees supporting a person affected by family violence Professional development development programs and resources to grow knowledge and skills Education Assistance Program featuring study and exam leave and up to 50% course fee reimbursement leadership courses and learning workshops opportunities for advancement and secondments into other Council roles Diversity and inclusion We’re committed to a diverse, inclusive and connected workplace where people feel safe, supported and valued for who they are. This includes people with disability, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people from diverse cultural and faith backgrounds, people of all ages, and people of diverse sexual orientations, genders and identities. Our Workforce Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Strategy 2025–2029 guides this work, but it’s our people, relationships and everyday actions that bring it to life. Employees are encouraged to connect through staff‐led groups and activities and help shape a workplace where everyone feels a sense of belonging and can thrive. Gender equity We’re committed to creating a workplace and community where people of all genders can thrive. Our Gender Equality Action Plan 2026–2030 focuses on fair and inclusive recruitment and career pathways, a safe and respectful workplace, and strong leadership and systems. We track progress regularly and report publicly every two years to the Commission for Gender Equality in the Public Sector. What this means for you: You’ll work in a fair, safe and inclusive workplace with transparent career pathways, supportive leadership and flexible work options. Keep up to date on what's happening at Yarra City Council, by following us on LinkedIn . Footer Subscribe by email Subscribe by email Council Your Say Yarra Council meetings Your councillors About Yarra Events News Services Rates Bin collection Parking permit application Planning permit application Pet registration More services Places Parks Libraries Leisure centres Childcare centres Neighbourhood houses Contact Online services (03) 9205 5555 Customer service centres Get help in your language Careers Yarra City Council acknowledges the Wurundjeri Woi Wurrung people as the Traditional Owners and true sovereigns of the land now known as Yarra. We also acknowledge the significant contributions made by other Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people to life in Yarra. We pay our respects to Elders from all nations - and to their Elders past, present and future. Privacy Policy Terms of Use Accessibility Return to Top Yarra City Council acknowledges the Wurundjeri Woi Wurrung people as the Traditional Owners and true sovereigns of the land now known as Yarra. We also acknowledge the significant contributions made by other Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people to life in Yarra. We pay our respects to Elders from all nations - and to their Elders past, present and future. Close panel Expand/Collapse Back to top menu Residents Expand/Collapse Living in Yarra Child, youth and family services People with disability 50 Plus Neighbourhood houses and learning centres Community safety and wellbeing Bins, waste, recycling and cleansing Transport Plants and trees Pets and animals Rates and valuations Diversity and inclusion Expand/Collapse Back to top menu Business Expand/Collapse Business in Yarra Events and training Services and support Economic research Centres and spaces Circular economy Waste collection Rates and valuations Accessibility Communities, groups and forums Yarra City Jobs Council tenders Register as one of our suppliers Permits, licences and registrations Food safety information Grants and funding Expand/Collapse Back to top menu Get involved Expand/Collapse Have your say Committees, meetings and minutes Take climate action Volunteering in Yarra Community awards Yarra Community Grants Program Community training Report an issue Expand/Collapse Back to top menu Plan