    {
      "advertised_salary_max": 121359.0,
      "advertised_salary_min": 108546.0,
      "advertised_salary_period": "week",
      "advertised_salary_text": "Jobs | Yarra City Council Skip to main content Search Menu Close Home Jobs Jobs Home Jobs Existing applicant login Subscribe to job alerts Job search Refine search Work type Full Time - Permanent 1 Locations Melbourne 1 Categories Services 1 Enterprise Project Management Officer (EPMO) Apply now Job no: 496804 Work type: Full Time - Permanent Location: Melbourne Categories: Services Enterprise Project Management Officer Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Band 7 – Starting from $108,546 – $121,359 + super + RDO ( RDO applicable for full-time 38 hours per week only ) Why You’ll Want to Join Us Supportive and friendly team environment where we value growth and development Hybrid/flexible working arrangements and an emphasis on work/life balance Work in a dynamic and collaborative environment Benefits Package Hybrid Working Policy For those working full time hours - 3 days worked in the office and 2 days WFH Exceptional leave entitlements - 16 days personal leave, 18 weeks parental leave, plus cultural leave and compassionate leave Health and wellbeing - free EAP counselling, discounted leisure membership 40% off for Staff and 25% off for Managers, salary sacrifice childcare options Professional Development – leadership courses and learning workshops, Education Assistance Program featuring study and exam leave and up to 50% course fee reimbursement About the Role We are seeking an experienced and proactive Enterprise Project Management Officer to support enterprise-wide project delivery and the uplift of project management capability across Council. Working within a dynamic environment, this role plays a key part in strengthening governance, improving consistency and contributing towards the successful delivery of Council’s Capital Works Program and Corporate Initiatives. You will partner with project managers, business units and senior stakeholders to drive best practice project management, reporting and assurance. We’re proud to offer flexible working arrangements, strong internal development pathways, and a culture that prioritises wellbeing and connection. This is a great opportunity for project management specialists, with hands-on learning, mentorship and future career progression opportunities. What We’re Looking For We are looking for a collaborative and detail-oriented professional with strong experience in project governance or PMO functions, ideally within a complex or public sector environment. You will bring a solid understanding of project management and a passion for improving systems and ways of working. With excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills, you can confidently support and influence teams across the organisation while delivering clear, high-quality reporting and insights. You are analytical, proactive and committed to continuous improvement, with the ability to balance strategic thinking and hands-on support to drive consistent, effective project delivery across Council. Yarra City Council is a Dynamic Organisation, proud of our inclusive culture . We strive to continually improve services to the community . Need More Info? For further information, please refer to the Position Description or contact Natasha Bengura , Acting Senior Coordinator Asset Management and Capital Works at natasha.bengura@yarracity.vic.gov.au . 404203 - Enterprise Project Management Officer - Position Description April 2026 - HR Final.pdf Applications close on: 12 June 2026, at 11:55pm How to Apply In your application, please include your Resume and a 1-page Cover Letter . In your cover letter, provide a brief overview addressing the Key Selection Criteria as outlined in the Position Description. A separate document addressing KSC is not required. Additional Information This position is subject to satisfactory Police Check prior to commencement. Pre-employment checks are not used by Yarra City Council to prevent any applicant from applying for this position. Each application will be considered on its merits. At Yarra Every Job is a Climate Job! Acting on the climate emergency requires that we change the way we think, make decisions, and prioritise action. We must embed proactive climate responses in the ways we govern, live our lives, and conduct our work. Every choice we make today and into the future will have an impact; this is true for Council and the community. Acknowledging the scale of this crisis, at Yarra we are committed to ensuring that every job is a climate job meaning that each staff member will play a key role in shaping our climate response. Yarra's Commitment to Diversity Yarra City Council is committed to being a child safe organisation and supports flexible and accessible working arrangements for all. This includes people with a disability, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, culturally, religiously and linguistically diverse people, young people, older people, women, and people who identify as gay, lesbian, bisexual, transgender, intersex or queer. We draw pride and strength from our diversity, remain open to new approaches and actively foster an inclusive workplace that celebrates the contribution made by all our people. Advertised: 22 May 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 12 Jun 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Search results Position Location Closes Enterprise Project Management Officer (EPMO) Melbourne 12 Jun 2026 Seeking a collaborative, detail-oriented PMO professional with strong governance experience to support enterprise project delivery and uplift capability. Expression of interest Loading... Current opportunities Position Location Closes Enterprise Project Management Officer (EPMO) Melbourne 12 Jun 2026 Seeking a collaborative, detail-oriented PMO professional with strong governance experience to support enterprise project delivery and uplift capability. Powered by PageUp Footer Subscribe by email Subscribe by