      "advertised_salary_period": "week",
      "advertised_salary_text": "Jobs | Yarra City Council Skip to main content Search Menu Close Home Jobs Jobs Home Jobs Existing applicant login Subscribe to job alerts Job search Refine search Work type Full Time - Permanent 1 Locations Melbourne 1 Categories Community 1 North Carlton Early Years Learning Precinct Team Leader Apply now Job no: 496802 Work type: Full Time - Permanent Location: Melbourne Categories: Community North Yarra Early Years Precinct Team Leader Family Youth & Children's Services Permanent Full Time Band 6 - Starting from $97,222.14 + super + RDO ( RDO applicable for full-time 38 hours per week only ) + Retention Payment to November 2026 Benefits Package Exceptional leave entitlements - 16 days personal leave, 18 weeks parental leave, plus cultural leave and compassionate leave Health and wellbeing - free EAP counselling, discounted leisure membership 40% off for staff and 25% off for managers, salary sacrifice childcare options Professional Development – leadership courses and learning workshops About the Role A rare and exciting opportunity is waiting for a highly experienced Early Years Learning Team Leader in the North Carlton and Princes Hill area. The role will encompass the team leadership of North Carlton Children’s Centre and Princes Hill Kindergarten. North Carlton Children’s Centre is licensed for 89 places, which encompasses two 0–3-year-old rooms, one integrated kindergarten program and one sessional kindergarten room that delivers 3- and 4-year-old sessional programs. Princes Hill Kindergarten is situated inside Princes Hill Primary School, is licensed for 22 children per day and currently delivering two mixed aged sessional programs. Pedagogy and Practice principles in our services are founded on the values of inclusion, voice of the child, trauma informed practice, environmental sustainability and meeting the individual needs of children and families. To support the team of highly dedicated educators, the Team Leader will sit within a leadership team comprising of the following: A full-time Early Learning Precinct Coordinator A full-time off the floor Precinct Team Leader A full-time off the floor Precinct Educational Leader Yarra is committed to exploring and implementing the latest approaches to pedagogy with a particular focus on inclusion and body safety. Yarra is also committed to offering the best conditions to our educators including: Above award remuneration Excellent conditions Leadership development and investment in succession planning Thorough induction and on-boarding process Enshrined non-contact time for all educators Access to ongoing professional development including internal and external training 2 child free days for whole unit professional development 3 child free days for commencement and close down preparations Excellent resource budgets for nutritious menus, room resources and centre resources Above industry standard management support at every level of the unit The qualities we are looking for in our candidate include A minimum 5 years’ experience in leadership/management roles in Education and Care services with particular strength in finance, compliance and human resource management Demonstrated understanding of and experience working with children and families with complex needs Ability to foster an environment of innovation amongst the team Proven experience with the planning and implementation of service projects Strong systems-thinking skills with the ability to design, implement and maintain effective operational processes Demonstrated numerical and analytical capability to develop and manage compliant rosters and staffing allocations Highly organised with strong time management skills, able to prioritise competing demands in a busy service environment Proven people management skills including the ability to support, coach and hold staff accountable in a respectful and strengths based way Ability to model professionalism and support others to meet expectations, deadlines and compliance requirements. For further information see the position description or contact Alysia Partridge, North Yarra Precinct Coordinator on (03) 92742710. 100680 - North Yarra Early Years Precinct Team Leader - Position Description - April 2025 (1).pdf How to Apply In your application, please include your Resume and a 1-page Cover Letter . In your cover letter, provide a brief overview addressing the Key Selection Criteria as outlined in the Position Description. A separate document addressing KSC is not required. Applications close on: Friday 29 May 2026, at 11:55pm At Yarra Every Job is a Climate Job! Acting on the climate emergency requires that we change the way we think, make decisions, and prioritise action. We must embed proactive climate responses in the ways we govern, live our lives, and conduct our work. Every choice we make today and into the future will have an impact; this is true for Council and the community. Acknowledging the scale of this crisis, at Yarra we are committed to ensuring that every job is a climate job meaning that each staff member will play a key role in shaping our climate response. Yarra's Commitment to Diversity Yarra City Council is committed to being a child safe organisation and supports flexible and accessible working arrangements for all. This includes people with a disability, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, culturally, religiously and linguistically diverse people, young people, older people, women, and people who identify as gay, lesbian, bisexual, transgender, intersex or queer. We draw pride and strength from our diversity, remain open to new approaches and actively foster an inclusive workplace that celebrates the contribution made by all our people. ( RDO applicable for full-time 38 hours per week only ) Advertised: 06 May 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 29 May 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Search results Position Location Closes North Carlton Early Years Learning Precinct Team Leader Melbourne 29 May 2026 Join Yarra as a highly experienced Early Years Learning Team Leader in the North Carlton and Princes Hill area to lead staff, manage services, and drive outcomes. Expression of interest Loading... Current opportunities Position Location Closes North Carlton Early Years Learning Precinct Team Leader Melbourne 29 May 2026 Join Yarra as a highly experienced Early Years Learning Team Leader in the North Carlton and Princes Hill area to lead staff, manage services, and drive outcomes. Powered by PageUp Footer Subscribe by email Subscribe by email Council Your Say Yarra Council meetings Your councillors About Yarra Events News Services Rates Bin collection Parking permit application Planning permit application Pet registration More services Places Parks Libraries Leisure centres Childcare centres Neighbourhood houses Contact Online services (03) 9205 5555 Customer service centres Get help in your language Careers Yarra City Council acknowledges the Wurundjeri Woi Wurrung people as the Traditional Owners and true sovereigns of the land now known as Yarra. We also acknowledge the significant contributions made by other Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people to life in Yarra. We pay our respects to Elders from all nations - and to their Elders past, present and future. Privacy Policy Terms of Use Accessibility Return to Top Yarra City Council acknowledges the Wurundjeri Woi Wurrung people as the Traditional Owners and true sovereigns of the land now known as Yarra. We also acknowledge the significant contributions made by other Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people to life in Yarra. We pay our respects to Elders from all nations - and to their Elders past, present and future. Close panel Expand/Collapse Back to top menu Residents Expand/Collapse Living in Yarra Child, youth and family services People with disability 50 Plus Neighbourhood