      "advertised_salary_text": "Jobs | Yarra City Council Skip to main content Search Menu Close Home Jobs Jobs Home Jobs Existing applicant login Subscribe to job alerts Job search Refine search Work type Casual 1 Locations Melbourne 1 Categories Community 1 Group Exercise Instructor Apply now Job no: 496532 Work type: Casual Location: Melbourne Categories: Community Apply anytime – this Expression Of Interest remains open year-round. We’re excited to connect with positive, motivated instructors who want to make a difference – one class at a time! Group Exercise Instructor Casual - Band 3A + 25% - $42.00 p/h + super + Class Allowance between $46.48 – $70.48 (class dependent) Yarra Leisure is on the lookout for energetic, enthusiastic and knowledgeable Group Exercise Instructors to work in our growing group exercise program. An ability to provide enjoyable, safe and fun classes is essential, as is the willingness to contribute to our positive team culture. We offer the latest equipment and technology to support you delivering current fitness trends. We deliver over 130 classes per week across our iconic Fitzroy, Collingwood and Richmond sites. Class styles we are recruiting for include: Aqua Deep Water Running Mat Pilates HIIT 45 Circuit Spin Zumba Yoga Meditation Tai Chi SwimFit Coaches for Adult Swimming Exercise What can we offer you: The latest equipment, technology and a supportive environment so you can deliver the very best classes. City of Yarra funded professional development and training opportunities, online and live courses for developing skills and secondment opportunities to advance your career. City of Yarra funded CPR, First Aid and CEC Courses. Complimentary membership - Gym, Swim and Group Exercise classes. If successful in joining Yarra Leisure and Yarra City Council, you'll be a key team member delivering a broad range of group exercise classes across our three modern leisure centres. Our extensive group fitness timetable is focused on health and wellbeing and caters to a wide range of participants. We pride ourselves on actively making a positive difference to the people within our community. What you need to apply: Ability to deliver enjoyable, safe and fun classes and the willingness to contribute to our positive team culture. To apply please upload as separate documents to the correct location provided: Cover Letter Resume Attach and upload current: Qualification specific to the application exercise styles. CPR and First Aid certification. Working with Children Check. AusActive Registration or equivalent, or willingness to attain. Answers to the three Key Selection Criteria must also be submitted in the form provided. A minimum answer of a paragraph on each answer is suggested. Describe your experience and ability to lead enjoyable, informative and productive exercise classes. Provide an example of your proactive ability to increase class participation and occupancy. Describe how you demonstrate commitment to ongoing professional development, maintenance of industry certifications and best practise techniques. For further details about the role, please see the Position Description or contact Adam Horton Group Exercise Team Leader adam.horton@yarracity.vic.gov.au 100459 - Group Exercise Instructor - Position Description (August 2025).pdf In your application, the selection panel will assess your CV against the technical skills, abilities, and qualifications of the Position Description as well as your separate responses to the Key Selection Criteria; including specific examples for each KSC. *This position is subject to satisfactory Police Check, Working with Children Check and a pre-employment medical assessment prior to commencement. Pre-employment checks are not used by Yarra City Council to prevent any applicant from applying for this position. Each application will be considered on its merits. Yarra City Council is committed to being a child safe organisation and supports flexible and accessible working arrangements for all. This includes people with a disability, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, culturally, religiously and linguistically diverse people, young people, older people, women, and people who identify as gay, lesbian, bisexual, transgender, intersex or queer. We draw pride and strength from our diversity, remain open to new approaches and actively foster an inclusive workplace that celebrates the contribution made by all our people. Advertised: 13 Aug 2025 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Search results Position Location Closes Group Exercise Instructor Melbourne Apply anytime – this EOI remains open year-round. We’re excited to connect with positive, motivated instructors who want to make a difference – one class at a time! Expression of interest Loading... Current opportunities Position Location Closes Group Exercise Instructor Melbourne Apply anytime – this EOI remains open year-round. We’re excited to connect with positive, motivated instructors who want to make a difference – one class at a time! Powered by PageUp Footer Subscribe by email Subscribe by email Council Your Say Yarra Council meetings Your councillors About Yarra Events News Services Rates Bin collection Parking permit application Planning permit application Pet registration More services Places Parks Libraries Leisure centres Childcare centres Neighbourhood houses Contact Online services (03) 9205 5555 Customer service centres Get help in your language Careers Yarra City Council acknowledges the Wurundjeri Woi Wurrung people as the Traditional Owners and true sovereigns of the land now known as Yarra. We also acknowledge the significant contributions made by other Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people to life in Yarra. We pay our respects to Elders from all nations - and to their Elders past, present and future. Privacy Policy Terms of Use Accessibility Return to Top Yarr